window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b098-8cd36557b17c6e1a.json"]={sha256:"8cd36557b17c6e1a9bf36f0ce703529cae6b94d6ff415d458c9d8a4627b75079",value:{"id":"b098","title":"建築雷射掃描竣工比對","titleEn":"Laser-scan verification of as-built construction","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從竣工偏差與量測不確定度出發，說明 USIBD LOA 的量測與表現精度、掃描儀測距誤差與點間距、標靶控制與配準，再處理依施工節點排定掃描、樓板平整度、點雲與模型偏差分析、獨立檢核點與 ISO 17123-9 檢定，最後談基準掃描、變形比對與 E57 資料交接，並以巴黎聖母院與烏干達卡蘇比王陵的掃描紀錄支持重建為例。","summaryEn":"Starting from as-built deviation and measurement uncertainty, explain measured and represented accuracy under the USIBD LOA specification, scanner ranging errors and point spacing, target control and registration, then scheduling scans at construction milestones, slab flatness, cloud-to-model deviation analysis, independent check points and ISO 17123-9 testing, and finally baseline scans, change detection and E57 data handover, using the scan records that supported rebuilding at Notre-Dame de Paris and the Kasubi Tombs in Uganda.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-facade-digital","subcategoryTitle":"帷幕牆、垂直運輸與數位營建","subcategoryTitleEn":"Facades, vertical transport and digital construction","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-facade-digital","learningTags":["structures","st-facade-digital","survey"],"architectureFamily":"survey","architectureNodes":[["掃描規劃與精度規格","Scan planning and accuracy specification"],["掃描儀與標靶控制","Scanners and target control"],["點雲配準與定位","Registration and georeferencing"],["模型偏差分析","Model deviation analysis"],["不符合事項與修正","Nonconformance and correction"],["點雲典藏與資產交接","Point-cloud archive and asset handover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,0],[3,5],[2,5]],"diagram":{"type":"survey","labels":["掃描規劃與精度規格","掃描儀與標靶控制","點雲配準與定位","模型偏差分析","不符合事項與修正"],"labelsEn":["Scan planning and accuracy specification","Scanners and target control","Registration and georeferencing","Model deviation analysis","Nonconformance and correction"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：一棟 30 層建築以掃描檢查帷幕牆托架位置，每層 40 個托架點、共 1,200 點，相對設計位置的偏差平均 +6 mm、標準差 8 mm（假設常態分布且已含量測誤差），托架可調範圍 ±20 mm。超出範圍的機率 = P(z > (20−6)/8 = 1.75) + P(z \u003c (−20−6)/8 = −3.25) ≈ 0.0401 + 0.0006 ≈ 0.041，約 1,200×0.041 ≈ 49 個托架需另做處理。若依掃描結果把帷幕牆安裝基準整體平移 6 mm，使平均偏差歸零，超出機率變為 P(|z| > 20/8 = 2.5) ≈ 0.012，只剩約 15 個。竣工掃描的價值不只在判定合格，更在讓下一工序依實際幾何調整基準；但基準調整須由帷幕牆設計者確認不影響室內淨距與接縫寬度。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際專案。","textEn":"Design exercise: curtain-wall bracket positions on a 30-storey building are checked by scanning, 40 bracket points per floor and 1,200 in all, with deviations from design averaging +6 mm and a standard deviation of 8 mm (assumed normal and including measurement error), against a bracket adjustment range of ±20 mm. The probability of falling outside is P(z > (20−6)/8 = 1.75) + P(z \u003c (−20−6)/8 = −3.25) ≈ 0.0401 + 0.0006 ≈ 0.041, so about 1,200×0.041 ≈ 49 brackets need special treatment. Shifting the whole façade setting-out datum by 6 mm according to the scan, so that the mean deviation becomes zero, changes the probability to P(|z| > 20/8 = 2.5) ≈ 0.012, leaving only about 15. The value of as-built scanning lies not only in judging conformance but in letting the next trade adjust its datum to actual geometry; the datum shift must still be confirmed by the façade designer as not affecting internal clearances or joint widths. Values are teaching assumptions, not any real project.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b098-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何」與「量測精度、表現精度與規格制定」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning\" and \"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b098-v13-01","title":"為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「竣工偏差與量測不確定度」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “As-built deviation and measurement uncertainty” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"設計模型描述的是理想幾何，實際完成的結構總有偏差：柱子傾斜、樓板高低不平、樓板邊緣進出、預埋件偏位。帷幕牆、電梯導軌、預製機電與裝修都依賴實際幾何，所以竣工驗證不是為了存檔，而是判斷偏差是否在公差內、下一工序能否吸收。雷射掃描一次取得數百萬點，能把整個樓層的偏差畫成分布圖；但量測本身也有不確定度，判定合格與否時必須讓量測不確定度明顯小於公差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「竣工偏差與量測不確定度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The design model describes ideal geometry, while the finished structure always deviates: columns lean, slabs undulate, slab edges wander and embeds shift. Curtain walls, lift rails, prefabricated services and fit-out all depend on the actual geometry, so as-built verification is not for the archive but for deciding whether deviations are within tolerance and whether the next trade can absorb them. Laser scanning captures millions of points at once and can map deviations over a whole floor, but the measurement itself is uncertain, and conformance decisions require that uncertainty to be clearly smaller than the tolerance. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “As-built deviation and measurement uncertainty” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：公差 ±10 mm，若要求量測不確定度比 4:1，95% 不確定度須 ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a ±10 mm tolerance and a 4:1 uncertainty ratio, the 95% measurement uncertainty must be ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「點雲有數百萬個點，所以每一點都比全測站量測更準確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A point cloud has millions of points, so every point is more accurate than a total-station measurement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「竣工偏差與量測不確定度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “As-built deviation and measurement uncertainty”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-01-k1","title":"為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何","titleEn":"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning","text":"設計模型描述的是理想幾何，實際完成的結構總有偏差：柱子傾斜、樓板高低不平、樓板邊緣進出、預埋件偏位。帷幕牆、電梯導軌、預製機電與裝修都依賴實際幾何，所以竣工驗證不是為了存檔，而是判斷偏差是否在公差內、下一工序能否吸收。","textEn":"The design model describes ideal geometry, while the finished structure always deviates: columns lean, slabs undulate, slab edges wander and embeds shift. Curtain walls, lift rails, prefabricated services and fit-out all depend on the actual geometry, so as-built verification is not for the archive but for deciding whether deviations are within tolerance and whether the next trade can absorb them.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：點雲有數百萬個點，所以每一點都比全測站量測更準確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A point cloud has millions of points, so every point is more accurate than a total-station measurement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning\" is correct?","options":["點雲有數百萬個點，所以每一點都比全測站量測更準確。","設計模型描述的是理想幾何，實際完成的結構總有偏差：柱子傾斜、樓板高低不平、樓板邊緣進出、預埋件偏位。","點雲精度很高，由它建立的模型自然也同樣精確。"],"optionsEn":["A point cloud has millions of points, so every point is more accurate than a total-station measurement.","The design model describes ideal geometry, while the finished structure always deviates: columns lean, slabs undulate, slab edges wander and embeds shift.","If the point cloud is accurate, the model built from it is automatically just as accurate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"設計模型描述的是理想幾何，實際完成的結構總有偏差：柱子傾斜、樓板高低不平、樓板邊緣進出、預埋件偏位。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The design model describes ideal geometry, while the finished structure always deviates: columns lean, slabs undulate, slab edges wander and embeds shift. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b098-v13-02","title":"為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何：定量估算","titleEn":"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「竣工偏差與量測不確定度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “As-built deviation and measurement uncertainty” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：公差 ±10 mm，若要求量測不確定度比 4:1，95% 不確定度須 ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm。若配準後點雲的 95% 不確定度為 6 mm，比值只有 10/6 ≈ 1.7，應設保護帶：量到的偏差 ≤ 10 − 6 = 4 mm 才判定合格，介於 4 至 16 mm 為不確定，需以全測站補測。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a ±10 mm tolerance and a 4:1 uncertainty ratio, the 95% measurement uncertainty must be ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm. If the registered cloud's 95% uncertainty is 6 mm, the ratio is only 10/6 ≈ 1.7, so a guard band applies: accept only measured deviations ≤ 10 − 6 = 4 mm, treat 4 to 16 mm as inconclusive and re-measure by total station. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在掃描計畫中為每一類元素寫明公差、所需量測不確定度與含保護帶的判定規則，掃描後以獨立檢核點估計實際不確定度；判定結果分為合格、不合格與不確定三類，不確定者以更高精度方法複測，而不是直接歸為合格。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: In the scan plan, state for each element type the tolerance, the required measurement uncertainty and the decision rule including guard bands, and after scanning estimate actual uncertainty from independent check points; classify results as conforming, nonconforming or inconclusive, re-measuring the inconclusive ones by a more accurate method rather than treating them as conforming.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"公差 ±10 mm，若要求量測不確定度比 4:1，95% 不確定度須 ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm。若配準後點雲的 95% 不確定度為 6 mm，比值只有 10/6 ≈ 1.7，應設保護帶：量到的偏差 ≤ 10 − 6 = 4 mm 才判定合格，介於 4 至 16 mm 為不確定，需以全測站補測。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a ±10 mm tolerance and a 4:1 uncertainty ratio, the 95% measurement uncertainty must be ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm. If the registered cloud's 95% uncertainty is 6 mm, the ratio is only 10/6 ≈ 1.7, so a guard band applies: accept only measured deviations ≤ 10 − 6 = 4 mm, treat 4 to 16 mm as inconclusive and re-measure by total station. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning\", which statement holds?","options":["自動配準軟體顯示誤差很小，點雲位置就一定正確。","樓板澆置完成後形狀就固定不變，何時量測都一樣。","公差 ±10 mm，若要求量測不確定度比 4:1，95% 不確定度須 ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm。"],"optionsEn":["If automatic registration reports small errors, the cloud must be correctly positioned.","Once a slab is poured its shape is fixed, so it does not matter when it is measured.","For a ±10 mm tolerance and a 4:1 uncertainty ratio, the 95% measurement uncertainty must be ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"公差 ±10 mm，若要求量測不確定度比 4:1，95% 不確定度須 ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a ±10 mm tolerance and a 4:1 uncertainty ratio, the 95% measurement uncertainty must be ≤ 10/4 = 2.5 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b098-v13-03","title":"為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「竣工偏差與量測不確定度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “As-built deviation and measurement uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在掃描計畫中為每一類元素寫明公差、所需量測不確定度與含保護帶的判定規則，掃描後以獨立檢核點估計實際不確定度；判定結果分為合格、不合格與不確定三類，不確定者以更高精度方法複測，而不是直接歸為合格。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"In the scan plan, state for each element type the tolerance, the required measurement uncertainty and the decision rule including guard bands, and after scanning estimate actual uncertainty from independent check points; classify results as conforming, nonconforming or inconclusive, re-measuring the inconclusive ones by a more accurate method rather than treating them as conforming. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：合約應寫明竣工驗證的判定規則與量測不確定度要求，並約定不確定結果的處理方式；判定不合格的元素由設計者評估可否接受或需修正，結論須書面化。","observationEn":"Site practice: The contract should state decision rules and measurement-uncertainty requirements for as-built verification and agree how inconclusive results are handled; elements judged nonconforming are assessed by the designer for acceptance or correction, with the decision in writing.","failure":"注意干擾：以 ±6 mm 不確定度的點雲判定 ±10 mm 公差的錨栓，報告宣稱全部合格，鋼柱吊裝時卻有數支對不上；反之也可能把合格構件誤判為不合格，造成不必要的打除與爭議。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Judging ±10 mm anchor bolts from a cloud with ±6 mm uncertainty yields a report declaring every bolt compliant, yet several steel columns will not fit at erection; the reverse error can also condemn compliant work, causing needless demolition and disputes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在掃描計畫中為每一類元素寫明公差、所需量測不確定度與含保護帶的判定規則，掃描後以獨立檢核點估計實際不確定度；判定結果分為合格、不合格與不確定三類，不確定者以更高精度方法複測，而不是直接歸為合格。","textEn":"In the scan plan, state for each element type the tolerance, the required measurement uncertainty and the decision rule including guard bands, and after scanning estimate actual uncertainty from independent check points; classify results as conforming, nonconforming or inconclusive, re-measuring the inconclusive ones by a more accurate method rather than treating them as conforming.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"合約應寫明竣工驗證的判定規則與量測不確定度要求，並約定不確定結果的處理方式；判定不合格的元素由設計者評估可否接受或需修正，結論須書面化。","textEn":"The contract should state decision rules and measurement-uncertainty requirements for as-built verification and agree how inconclusive results are handled; elements judged nonconforming are assessed by the designer for acceptance or correction, with the decision in writing.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning\"?","options":["在掃描計畫中為每一類元素寫明公差、所需量測不確定度與含保護帶的判定規則，掃描後以獨立檢核點估計實際不確定度。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","配準軟體報告的誤差就是點雲的絕對精度。"],"optionsEn":["In the scan plan, state for each element type the tolerance, the required measurement uncertainty and the decision rule including guard bands, and after scanning estimate actual uncertainty from independent check points.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The error reported by registration software is the absolute accuracy of the cloud."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在掃描計畫中為每一類元素寫明公差、所需量測不確定度與含保護帶的判定規則，掃描後以獨立檢核點估計實際不確定度；判定結果分為合格、不合格與不確定三類，不確定者以更高精度方法複測，而不是直接歸為合格。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"In the scan plan, state for each element type the tolerance, the required measurement uncertainty and the decision rule including guard bands, and after scanning estimate actual uncertainty from independent check points; classify results as conforming, nonconforming or inconclusive, re-measuring the inconclusive ones by a more accurate method rather than treating them as conforming. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b098-v13-04","title":"為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何：失效診斷","titleEn":"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「竣工偏差與量測不確定度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “As-built deviation and measurement uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以 ±6 mm 不確定度的點雲判定 ±10 mm 公差的錨栓，報告宣稱全部合格，鋼柱吊裝時卻有數支對不上；反之也可能把合格構件誤判為不合格，造成不必要的打除與爭議。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Judging ±10 mm anchor bolts from a cloud with ±6 mm uncertainty yields a report declaring every bolt compliant, yet several steel columns will not fit at erection; the reverse error can also condemn compliant work, causing needless demolition and disputes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：雷射掃描一次取得數百萬點，能把整個樓層的偏差畫成分布圖；但量測本身也有不確定度，判定合格與否時必須讓量測不確定度明顯小於公差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Laser scanning captures millions of points at once and can map deviations over a whole floor, but the measurement itself is uncertain, and conformance decisions require that uncertainty to be clearly smaller than the tolerance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「點雲有數百萬個點，所以每一點都比全測站量測更準確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A point cloud has millions of points, so every point is more accurate than a total-station measurement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以 ±6 mm 不確定度的點雲判定 ±10 mm 公差的錨栓，報告宣稱全部合格，鋼柱吊裝時卻有數支對不上；反之也可能把合格構件誤判為不合格，造成不必要的打除與爭議。","textEn":"Judging ±10 mm anchor bolts from a cloud with ±6 mm uncertainty yields a report declaring every bolt compliant, yet several steel columns will not fit at erection; the reverse error can also condemn compliant work, causing needless demolition and disputes.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「為何以掃描驗證竣工幾何」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Why verify as-built geometry by scanning\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","以 ±6 mm 不確定度的點雲判定 ±10 mm 公差的錨栓，報告宣稱全部合格，鋼柱吊裝時卻有數支對不上。","點雲精度很高，由它建立的模型自然也同樣精確。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Judging ±10 mm anchor bolts from a cloud with ±6 mm uncertainty yields a report declaring every bolt compliant, yet several steel columns will not fit at erection.","If the point cloud is accurate, the model built from it is automatically just as accurate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以 ±6 mm 不確定度的點雲判定 ±10 mm 公差的錨栓，報告宣稱全部合格，鋼柱吊裝時卻有數支對不上；反之也可能把合格構件誤判為不合格，造成不必要的打除與爭議。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Judging ±10 mm anchor bolts from a cloud with ±6 mm uncertainty yields a report declaring every bolt compliant, yet several steel columns will not fit at erection; the reverse error can also condemn compliant work, causing needless demolition and disputes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b098-v13-05","title":"量測精度、表現精度與規格制定：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「LOA 精度等級」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “LOA accuracy level” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"美國建築文件協會（USIBD）的 LOA 規範把精度分成兩種：量測精度是點雲本身相對於控制的精度，表現精度是由點雲擷取或建立的模型、圖面相對於真實位置的精度。後者還包含擬合、簡化與建模者判斷的誤差，所以不可能優於前者。規範以標準差的倍數（約 2σ）表示等級，並鼓勵依元素指定，例如結構柱與帷幕牆埋件要求較高、一般隔間要求較低，而不是整棟建築套用單一數字。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「LOA 精度等級」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The USIBD LOA Specification separates two accuracies: measured accuracy is that of the point cloud itself relative to control, and represented accuracy is that of the models or drawings extracted from the cloud relative to true position. The latter adds errors from fitting, simplification and modeller judgement, so it can never be better than the former. The specification expresses levels as multiples of standard deviation, about 2σ, and encourages assigning them by element, for example tighter for structural columns and façade embeds and looser for ordinary partitions, rather than one number for the whole building. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “LOA accuracy level” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：點雲量測精度 2σ = 4 mm，建模擬合誤差 2σ = 6 mm，表現精度約 √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm（2σ）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With measured accuracy 2σ = 4 mm and modelling-fit error 2σ = 6 mm, represented accuracy is about √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm at 2σ.","failure":"常見誤解：「點雲精度很高，由它建立的模型自然也同樣精確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the point cloud is accurate, the model built from it is automatically just as accurate.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「LOA 精度等級」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “LOA accuracy level”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-05-k1","title":"量測精度、表現精度與規格制定","titleEn":"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification","text":"美國建築文件協會（USIBD）的 LOA 規範把精度分成兩種：量測精度是點雲本身相對於控制的精度，表現精度是由點雲擷取或建立的模型、圖面相對於真實位置的精度。後者還包含擬合、簡化與建模者判斷的誤差，所以不可能優於前者。","textEn":"The USIBD LOA Specification separates two accuracies: measured accuracy is that of the point cloud itself relative to control, and represented accuracy is that of the models or drawings extracted from the cloud relative to true position. The latter adds errors from fitting, simplification and modeller judgement, so it can never be better than the former.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：點雲精度很高，由它建立的模型自然也同樣精確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the point cloud is accurate, the model built from it is automatically just as accurate. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量測精度、表現精度與規格制定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification\" is correct?","options":["點雲精度很高，由它建立的模型自然也同樣精確。","掃描儀的標稱精度在任何距離與角度都一樣。","美國建築文件協會（USIBD）的 LOA 規範把精度分成兩種：量測精度是點雲本身相對於控制的精度，表現精度是由點雲擷取或建立的模型、圖面相對於真實位置的精度。"],"optionsEn":["If the point cloud is accurate, the model built from it is automatically just as accurate.","A scanner's nominal accuracy holds at every range and angle.","The USIBD LOA Specification separates two accuracies: measured accuracy is that of the point cloud itself relative to control, and represented accuracy is that of the models or drawings extracted from the cloud relative to true position."],"answer":2,"explanation":"美國建築文件協會（USIBD）的 LOA 規範把精度分成兩種：量測精度是點雲本身相對於控制的精度，表現精度是由點雲擷取或建立的模型、圖面相對於真實位置的精度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The USIBD LOA Specification separates two accuracies: measured accuracy is that of the point cloud itself relative to control, and represented accuracy is that of the models or drawings extracted from the cloud relative to true position. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b098-v13-06","title":"量測精度、表現精度與規格制定：定量估算","titleEn":"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「LOA 精度等級」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “LOA accuracy level” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：點雲量測精度 2σ = 4 mm，建模擬合誤差 2σ = 6 mm，表現精度約 √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm（2σ）。若元素公差 ±15 mm 而要求 4:1，表現精度須 ≤ 15/4 ≈ 3.75 mm，這組成果不足，需提高掃描密度並以幾何擬合取代手動描繪。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With measured accuracy 2σ = 4 mm and modelling-fit error 2σ = 6 mm, represented accuracy is about √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm at 2σ. If the element tolerance is ±15 mm with a 4:1 requirement, represented accuracy must be ≤ 15/4 ≈ 3.75 mm, so this result falls short and needs denser scanning and geometric fitting instead of manual tracing. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交付時分別提出量測精度報告（檢核點殘差）與表現精度報告（模型元素與點雲的距離統計），兩者都以 2σ 表示並與規格中每類元素的 LOA 等級比較；抽樣元素由第三方以全測站複測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At delivery provide separate reports for measured accuracy (check-point residuals) and represented accuracy (distance statistics between model elements and the cloud), both at 2σ and compared with the LOA level specified for each element class; a third party re-measures sampled elements by total station.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"點雲量測精度 2σ = 4 mm，建模擬合誤差 2σ = 6 mm，表現精度約 √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm（2σ）。若元素公差 ±15 mm 而要求 4:1，表現精度須 ≤ 15/4 ≈ 3.75 mm，這組成果不足，需提高掃描密度並以幾何擬合取代手動描繪。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With measured accuracy 2σ = 4 mm and modelling-fit error 2σ = 6 mm, represented accuracy is about √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm at 2σ. If the element tolerance is ±15 mm with a 4:1 requirement, represented accuracy must be ≤ 15/4 ≈ 3.75 mm, so this result falls short and needs denser scanning and geometric fitting instead of manual tracing. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「量測精度、表現精度與規格制定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification\", which statement holds?","options":["點雲量測精度 2σ = 4 mm，建模擬合誤差 2σ = 6 mm，表現精度約 √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm（2σ）。","竣工掃描可以等全部完工後一次做完就好。","偏差圖大部分是綠色，就代表竣工品質合格。"],"optionsEn":["With measured accuracy 2σ = 4 mm and modelling-fit error 2σ = 6 mm, represented accuracy is about √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm at 2σ.","As-built scanning can wait until everything is finished and be done once.","If the deviation map is mostly green, the as-built quality is acceptable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"點雲量測精度 2σ = 4 mm，建模擬合誤差 2σ = 6 mm，表現精度約 √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm（2σ）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With measured accuracy 2σ = 4 mm and modelling-fit error 2σ = 6 mm, represented accuracy is about √(4² + 6²) = √52 ≈ 7.2 mm at 2σ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b098-v13-07","title":"量測精度、表現精度與規格制定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「LOA 精度等級」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “LOA accuracy level” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交付時分別提出量測精度報告（檢核點殘差）與表現精度報告（模型元素與點雲的距離統計），兩者都以 2σ 表示並與規格中每類元素的 LOA 等級比較；抽樣元素由第三方以全測站複測。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At delivery provide separate reports for measured accuracy (check-point residuals) and represented accuracy (distance statistics between model elements and the cloud), both at 2σ and compared with the LOA level specified for each element class; a third party re-measures sampled elements by total station. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在掃描與建模規格中依元素類別分別指定量測與表現的 LOA 等級，並寫明採用的信賴水準；採購時要求廠商提出以往專案的檢核點報告作為能力證明。","observationEn":"Site practice: In the scanning and modelling specification assign measured and represented LOA levels by element class and state the confidence level used; at procurement ask firms for check-point reports from earlier projects as evidence of capability.","failure":"注意干擾：業主只寫「竣工模型精度 ±5 mm」而未區分量測與表現精度，掃描廠商交出高精度點雲，建模者卻以簡化牆體描繪，模型位置偏差達數公分，事後各方對責任歸屬爭執不下。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An owner who writes only ‘as-built model accuracy ±5 mm’ without separating measured and represented accuracy receives a precise cloud from the scanning firm, but the modeller traces simplified walls several centimetres off, and the parties then argue over responsibility. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交付時分別提出量測精度報告（檢核點殘差）與表現精度報告（模型元素與點雲的距離統計），兩者都以 2σ 表示並與規格中每類元素的 LOA 等級比較；抽樣元素由第三方以全測站複測。","textEn":"At delivery provide separate reports for measured accuracy (check-point residuals) and represented accuracy (distance statistics between model elements and the cloud), both at 2σ and compared with the LOA level specified for each element class; a third party re-measures sampled elements by total station.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在掃描與建模規格中依元素類別分別指定量測與表現的 LOA 等級，並寫明採用的信賴水準；採購時要求廠商提出以往專案的檢核點報告作為能力證明。","textEn":"In the scanning and modelling specification assign measured and represented LOA levels by element class and state the confidence level used; at procurement ask firms for check-point reports from earlier projects as evidence of capability.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「量測精度、表現精度與規格制定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","交付時分別提出量測精度報告（檢核點殘差）與表現精度報告（模型元素與點雲的距離統計），兩者都以 2σ 表示並與規格中每類元素的 LOA 等級比較。","兩期點雲直接相減，就能偵測到小於單點雜訊的變形。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","At delivery provide separate reports for measured accuracy (check-point residuals) and represented accuracy (distance statistics between model elements and the cloud), both at 2σ and compared with the LOA level specified for each element class.","Subtracting two point clouds directly detects deformation smaller than single-point noise."],"answer":1,"explanation":"交付時分別提出量測精度報告（檢核點殘差）與表現精度報告（模型元素與點雲的距離統計），兩者都以 2σ 表示並與規格中每類元素的 LOA 等級比較；抽樣元素由第三方以全測站複測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"At delivery provide separate reports for measured accuracy (check-point residuals) and represented accuracy (distance statistics between model elements and the cloud), both at 2σ and compared with the LOA level specified for each element class; a third party re-measures sampled elements by total station. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b098-v13-08","title":"量測精度、表現精度與規格制定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「LOA 精度等級」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “LOA accuracy level” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"業主只寫「竣工模型精度 ±5 mm」而未區分量測與表現精度，掃描廠商交出高精度點雲，建模者卻以簡化牆體描繪，模型位置偏差達數公分，事後各方對責任歸屬爭執不下。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An owner who writes only ‘as-built model accuracy ±5 mm’ without separating measured and represented accuracy receives a precise cloud from the scanning firm, but the modeller traces simplified walls several centimetres off, and the parties then argue over responsibility. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：規範以標準差的倍數（約 2σ）表示等級，並鼓勵依元素指定，例如結構柱與帷幕牆埋件要求較高、一般隔間要求較低，而不是整棟建築套用單一數字。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The specification expresses levels as multiples of standard deviation, about 2σ, and encourages assigning them by element, for example tighter for structural columns and façade embeds and looser for ordinary partitions, rather than one number for the whole building.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「點雲精度很高，由它建立的模型自然也同樣精確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the point cloud is accurate, the model built from it is automatically just as accurate.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"業主只寫「竣工模型精度 ±5 mm」而未區分量測與表現精度，掃描廠商交出高精度點雲，建模者卻以簡化牆體描繪，模型位置偏差達數公分，事後各方對責任歸屬爭執不下。","textEn":"An owner who writes only ‘as-built model accuracy ±5 mm’ without separating measured and represented accuracy receives a precise cloud from the scanning firm, but the modeller traces simplified walls several centimetres off, and the parties then argue over responsibility.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「量測精度、表現精度與規格制定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Measured accuracy, represented accuracy and specification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","掃描儀的標稱精度在任何距離與角度都一樣。","業主只寫「竣工模型精度 ±5 mm」而未區分量測與表現精度，掃描廠商交出高精度點雲，建模者卻以簡化牆體描繪，模型位置偏差達數公分，事後各方對責任歸屬爭執不下。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A scanner's nominal accuracy holds at every range and angle.","An owner who writes only ‘as-built model accuracy ±5 mm’ without separating measured and represented accuracy receives a precise cloud from the scanning firm, but the modeller traces simplified walls several centimetres off, and the parties then argue over responsibility."],"answer":2,"explanation":"業主只寫「竣工模型精度 ±5 mm」而未區分量測與表現精度，掃描廠商交出高精度點雲，建模者卻以簡化牆體描繪，模型位置偏差達數公分，事後各方對責任歸屬爭執不下。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An owner who writes only ‘as-built model accuracy ±5 mm’ without separating measured and represented accuracy receives a precise cloud from the scanning firm, but the modeller traces simplified walls several centimetres off, and the parties then argue over responsibility. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b098-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源」與「標靶、控制與點雲配準」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Scanner ranging principles and error sources\" and \"Targets, control and point-cloud registration\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b098-v13-09","title":"掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Scanner ranging principles and error sources: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「點間距與入射角」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Point spacing and incidence angle” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"地面雷射掃描儀以飛行時間或相位差量測距離，再配合水平與垂直角度編碼器得到每一點的三維坐標。點的品質隨距離、入射角與表面反射率改變：距離越遠、光束越斜，光斑越大、測距雜訊越高；深色、潮濕或鏡面材料回波弱或產生多路徑；光束同時打到前後兩個物體邊緣時會產生懸浮的混合點。掃描規劃因此要控制最大距離與入射角，而不是只看儀器的標稱精度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「點間距與入射角」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A terrestrial laser scanner measures range by time of flight or phase difference and, with horizontal and vertical angle encoders, gives three-dimensional coordinates for each point. Point quality varies with range, incidence angle and surface reflectivity: longer ranges and more oblique beams enlarge the footprint and raise range noise, dark, wet or mirror-like materials return weak signals or multipath, and a beam that clips the edges of two objects at different depths produces floating mixed points. Scan planning must therefore limit maximum range and incidence angle rather than relying on the nominal instrument accuracy. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Point spacing and incidence angle” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：點間距 s = R·Δθ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Point spacing s = R·Δθ.","failure":"常見誤解：「掃描儀的標稱精度在任何距離與角度都一樣。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A scanner's nominal accuracy holds at every range and angle.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「點間距與入射角」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Point spacing and incidence angle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-09-k1","title":"掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源","titleEn":"Scanner ranging principles and error sources","text":"地面雷射掃描儀以飛行時間或相位差量測距離，再配合水平與垂直角度編碼器得到每一點的三維坐標。點的品質隨距離、入射角與表面反射率改變：距離越遠、光束越斜，光斑越大、測距雜訊越高；深色、潮濕或鏡面材料回波弱或產生多路徑；光束同時打到前後兩個物體邊緣時會產生懸浮的混合點。","textEn":"A terrestrial laser scanner measures range by time of flight or phase difference and, with horizontal and vertical angle encoders, gives three-dimensional coordinates for each point. Point quality varies with range, incidence angle and surface reflectivity: longer ranges and more oblique beams enlarge the footprint and raise range noise, dark, wet or mirror-like materials return weak signals or multipath, and a beam that clips the edges of two objects at different depths produces floating mixed points.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：掃描儀的標稱精度在任何距離與角度都一樣。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A scanner's nominal accuracy holds at every range and angle. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scanner ranging principles and error sources\" is correct?","options":["地面雷射掃描儀以飛行時間或相位差量測距離，再配合水平與垂直角度編碼器得到每一點的三維坐標。","掃描儀的標稱精度在任何距離與角度都一樣。","自動配準軟體顯示誤差很小，點雲位置就一定正確。"],"optionsEn":["A terrestrial laser scanner measures range by time of flight or phase difference and, with horizontal and vertical angle encoders, gives three-dimensional coordinates for each point.","A scanner's nominal accuracy holds at every range and angle.","If automatic registration reports small errors, the cloud must be correctly positioned."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地面雷射掃描儀以飛行時間或相位差量測距離，再配合水平與垂直角度編碼器得到每一點的三維坐標。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A terrestrial laser scanner measures range by time of flight or phase difference and, with horizontal and vertical angle encoders, gives three-dimensional coordinates for each point. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b098-v13-10","title":"掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源：定量估算","titleEn":"Scanner ranging principles and error sources: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「點間距與入射角」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Point spacing and incidence angle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：點間距 s = R·Δθ。角度步距 0.036° = 6.28×10⁻⁴ rad：距離 20 m 時 s = 20×6.28×10⁻⁴ ≈ 12.6 mm，50 m 時約 31.4 mm；若入射角 70°，牆面上的點間距再放大 1/cos 70° ≈ 2.92 倍，20 m 處約 36.7 mm，可能漏掉 25 mm 寬埋件的邊緣。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Point spacing s = R·Δθ. With an angular step of 0.036° = 6.28×10⁻⁴ rad, s = 20×6.28×10⁻⁴ ≈ 12.6 mm at 20 m and about 31.4 mm at 50 m; at a 70° incidence angle the spacing on a wall grows by 1/cos 70° ≈ 2.92, to about 36.7 mm at 20 m, enough to miss the edge of a 25 mm wide embed. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：掃描前以平面圖規劃測站，確認每個需驗證的元素至少有一站在距離與入射角限制內；掃描後檢查點雲的點間距、雜訊（例如平面擬合殘差）與混合點，深色或反光表面以噴粉或標靶輔助，必要時加站補掃。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plan stations on the floor plan before scanning so that every element to be verified is seen by at least one station within the range and incidence limits; after scanning check point spacing, noise (for example plane-fit residuals) and mixed points, use spray or targets on dark or reflective surfaces, and add stations where needed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"點間距 s = R·Δθ。角度步距 0.036° = 6.28×10⁻⁴ rad：距離 20 m 時 s = 20×6.28×10⁻⁴ ≈ 12.6 mm，50 m 時約 31.4 mm；若入射角 70°，牆面上的點間距再放大 1/cos 70° ≈ 2.92 倍，20 m 處約 36.7 mm，可能漏掉 25 mm 寬埋件的邊緣。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Point spacing s = R·Δθ. With an angular step of 0.036° = 6.28×10⁻⁴ rad, s = 20×6.28×10⁻⁴ ≈ 12.6 mm at 20 m and about 31.4 mm at 50 m; at a 70° incidence angle the spacing on a wall grows by 1/cos 70° ≈ 2.92, to about 36.7 mm at 20 m, enough to miss the edge of a 25 mm wide embed. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scanner ranging principles and error sources\", which statement holds?","options":["樓板澆置完成後形狀就固定不變，何時量測都一樣。","點間距 s = R·Δθ。","配準軟體報告的誤差就是點雲的絕對精度。"],"optionsEn":["Once a slab is poured its shape is fixed, so it does not matter when it is measured.","Point spacing s = R·Δθ.","The error reported by registration software is the absolute accuracy of the cloud."],"answer":1,"explanation":"點間距 s = R·Δθ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Point spacing s = R·Δθ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b098-v13-11","title":"掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scanner ranging principles and error sources: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「點間距與入射角」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Point spacing and incidence angle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"掃描前以平面圖規劃測站，確認每個需驗證的元素至少有一站在距離與入射角限制內；掃描後檢查點雲的點間距、雜訊（例如平面擬合殘差）與混合點，深色或反光表面以噴粉或標靶輔助，必要時加站補掃。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plan stations on the floor plan before scanning so that every element to be verified is seen by at least one station within the range and incidence limits; after scanning check point spacing, noise (for example plane-fit residuals) and mixed points, use spray or targets on dark or reflective surfaces, and add stations where needed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：掃描作業程序要規定最大掃描距離、最大入射角與每類元素的最小點密度，在現場以快速預覽確認覆蓋率後才拆站，並事先列出反光或深色材料的處理方式。","observationEn":"Site practice: The scanning procedure should set maximum range, maximum incidence angle and minimum point density per element type, confirm coverage on a quick preview before striking each station, and list in advance how reflective or dark materials will be handled.","failure":"注意干擾：為了省時只在樓層中央架一站，遠端柱面以極斜角度被掃到，點雲稀疏且雜訊大，偏差分析把雜訊當成柱子歪斜而發出不合格通知，經全測站複測才確認是量測問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: To save time a single station is set up in the middle of the floor, so far column faces are hit at very oblique angles; the sparse, noisy cloud makes deviation analysis read noise as column lean and issue a nonconformance, which only a total-station re-measure exposes as a measurement artefact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"掃描前以平面圖規劃測站，確認每個需驗證的元素至少有一站在距離與入射角限制內；掃描後檢查點雲的點間距、雜訊（例如平面擬合殘差）與混合點，深色或反光表面以噴粉或標靶輔助，必要時加站補掃。","textEn":"Plan stations on the floor plan before scanning so that every element to be verified is seen by at least one station within the range and incidence limits; after scanning check point spacing, noise (for example plane-fit residuals) and mixed points, use spray or targets on dark or reflective surfaces, and add stations where needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"掃描作業程序要規定最大掃描距離、最大入射角與每類元素的最小點密度，在現場以快速預覽確認覆蓋率後才拆站，並事先列出反光或深色材料的處理方式。","textEn":"The scanning procedure should set maximum range, maximum incidence angle and minimum point density per element type, confirm coverage on a quick preview before striking each station, and list in advance how reflective or dark materials will be handled.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scanner ranging principles and error sources\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","點雲交出檔案就完成交接，不需要後設資料。","掃描前以平面圖規劃測站，確認每個需驗證的元素至少有一站在距離與入射角限制內。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Handing over the point-cloud files completes the handover; metadata is unnecessary.","Plan stations on the floor plan before scanning so that every element to be verified is seen by at least one station within the range and incidence limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"掃描前以平面圖規劃測站，確認每個需驗證的元素至少有一站在距離與入射角限制內；掃描後檢查點雲的點間距、雜訊（例如平面擬合殘差）與混合點，深色或反光表面以噴粉或標靶輔助，必要時加站補掃。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plan stations on the floor plan before scanning so that every element to be verified is seen by at least one station within the range and incidence limits; after scanning check point spacing, noise (for example plane-fit residuals) and mixed points, use spray or targets on dark or reflective surfaces, and add stations where needed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b098-v13-12","title":"掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scanner ranging principles and error sources: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「點間距與入射角」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Point spacing and incidence angle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為了省時只在樓層中央架一站，遠端柱面以極斜角度被掃到，點雲稀疏且雜訊大，偏差分析把雜訊當成柱子歪斜而發出不合格通知，經全測站複測才確認是量測問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"To save time a single station is set up in the middle of the floor, so far column faces are hit at very oblique angles; the sparse, noisy cloud makes deviation analysis read noise as column lean and issue a nonconformance, which only a total-station re-measure exposes as a measurement artefact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：掃描規劃因此要控制最大距離與入射角，而不是只看儀器的標稱精度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Scan planning must therefore limit maximum range and incidence angle rather than relying on the nominal instrument accuracy.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「掃描儀的標稱精度在任何距離與角度都一樣。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A scanner's nominal accuracy holds at every range and angle.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為了省時只在樓層中央架一站，遠端柱面以極斜角度被掃到，點雲稀疏且雜訊大，偏差分析把雜訊當成柱子歪斜而發出不合格通知，經全測站複測才確認是量測問題。","textEn":"To save time a single station is set up in the middle of the floor, so far column faces are hit at very oblique angles; the sparse, noisy cloud makes deviation analysis read noise as column lean and issue a nonconformance, which only a total-station re-measure exposes as a measurement artefact.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掃描儀測距原理與誤差來源」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scanner ranging principles and error sources\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["為了省時只在樓層中央架一站，遠端柱面以極斜角度被掃到，點雲稀疏且雜訊大，偏差分析把雜訊當成柱子歪斜而發出不合格通知，經全測站複測才確認是量測問題。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","自動配準軟體顯示誤差很小，點雲位置就一定正確。"],"optionsEn":["To save time a single station is set up in the middle of the floor, so far column faces are hit at very oblique angles.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If automatic registration reports small errors, the cloud must be correctly positioned."],"answer":0,"explanation":"為了省時只在樓層中央架一站，遠端柱面以極斜角度被掃到，點雲稀疏且雜訊大，偏差分析把雜訊當成柱子歪斜而發出不合格通知，經全測站複測才確認是量測問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"To save time a single station is set up in the middle of the floor, so far column faces are hit at very oblique angles; the sparse, noisy cloud makes deviation analysis read noise as column lean and issue a nonconformance, which only a total-station re-measure exposes as a measurement artefact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b098-v13-13","title":"標靶、控制與點雲配準：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Targets, control and point-cloud registration: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「球形標靶與控制點」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sphere targets and control points” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"每一站掃描都有自己的局部坐標，必須配準成一個整體並轉到工地坐標系，才能與設計模型比較。配準可利用球形或棋盤格標靶，也可用點雲重疊區域自動匹配；後者方便，但在長走廊或樓梯間這類幾何單調的空間容易沿長軸滑移，誤差也會沿測站鏈累積。以全測站測得的控制標靶把點雲綁到工地控制網，並保留不參與配準的檢核標靶，才能證明配準結果可信。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「球形標靶與控制點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each scan station has its own local coordinates, so stations must be registered into one cloud and transformed into the site coordinate system before comparison with the design model. Registration can use sphere or checkerboard targets or automatic matching of overlapping clouds; the latter is convenient but tends to slide along the long axis in geometrically plain spaces such as corridors and stairwells, and errors accumulate along a chain of stations. Tying the cloud to the site control network through targets surveyed by total station, and keeping check targets that take no part in registration, is what proves the registration trustworthy. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Sphere targets and control points” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：20 站以點雲匹配串聯，每一連接隨機誤差 2 mm，鏈末端累積約 √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm；若每 5 站以全測站控制標靶約束一次，累積僅約 √5×2 ≈ 4.5 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Chaining 20 stations by cloud matching with 2 mm random error per link accumulates about √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm at the end of the chain; constraining every fifth station with total-station control targets limits accumulation to about √5×2 ≈ 4.5 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「自動配準軟體顯示誤差很小，點雲位置就一定正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If automatic registration reports small errors, the cloud must be correctly positioned.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「球形標靶與控制點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Sphere targets and control points”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-13-k1","title":"標靶、控制與點雲配準","titleEn":"Targets, control and point-cloud registration","text":"每一站掃描都有自己的局部坐標，必須配準成一個整體並轉到工地坐標系，才能與設計模型比較。配準可利用球形或棋盤格標靶，也可用點雲重疊區域自動匹配；後者方便，但在長走廊或樓梯間這類幾何單調的空間容易沿長軸滑移，誤差也會沿測站鏈累積。","textEn":"Each scan station has its own local coordinates, so stations must be registered into one cloud and transformed into the site coordinate system before comparison with the design model. Registration can use sphere or checkerboard targets or automatic matching of overlapping clouds; the latter is convenient but tends to slide along the long axis in geometrically plain spaces such as corridors and stairwells, and errors accumulate along a chain of stations.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：自動配準軟體顯示誤差很小，點雲位置就一定正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If automatic registration reports small errors, the cloud must be correctly positioned. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「標靶、控制與點雲配準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Targets, control and point-cloud registration\" is correct?","options":["自動配準軟體顯示誤差很小，點雲位置就一定正確。","每一站掃描都有自己的局部坐標，必須配準成一個整體並轉到工地坐標系，才能與設計模型比較。","竣工掃描可以等全部完工後一次做完就好。"],"optionsEn":["If automatic registration reports small errors, the cloud must be correctly positioned.","Each scan station has its own local coordinates, so stations must be registered into one cloud and transformed into the site coordinate system before comparison with the design model.","As-built scanning can wait until everything is finished and be done once."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每一站掃描都有自己的局部坐標，必須配準成一個整體並轉到工地坐標系，才能與設計模型比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each scan station has its own local coordinates, so stations must be registered into one cloud and transformed into the site coordinate system before comparison with the design model. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b098-v13-14","title":"標靶、控制與點雲配準：定量估算","titleEn":"Targets, control and point-cloud registration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「球形標靶與控制點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sphere targets and control points” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：20 站以點雲匹配串聯，每一連接隨機誤差 2 mm，鏈末端累積約 √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm；若每 5 站以全測站控制標靶約束一次，累積僅約 √5×2 ≈ 4.5 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Chaining 20 stations by cloud matching with 2 mm random error per link accumulates about √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm at the end of the chain; constraining every fifth station with total-station control targets limits accumulation to about √5×2 ≈ 4.5 mm. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：配準報告須列出每個標靶與重疊區的殘差、整體平差統計與檢核標靶的偏差；檢核標靶由全測站獨立量測，偏差超過規格（例如 2σ 超出要求的 LOA 上限）時，該區點雲不得用於判定。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The registration report must list residuals for each target and overlap, overall adjustment statistics and deviations at check targets; check targets are measured independently by total station, and if their deviations exceed the specification, for example a 2σ beyond the required LOA bound, that part of the cloud may not be used for conformance decisions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"20 站以點雲匹配串聯，每一連接隨機誤差 2 mm，鏈末端累積約 √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm；若每 5 站以全測站控制標靶約束一次，累積僅約 √5×2 ≈ 4.5 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Chaining 20 stations by cloud matching with 2 mm random error per link accumulates about √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm at the end of the chain; constraining every fifth station with total-station control targets limits accumulation to about √5×2 ≈ 4.5 mm. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「標靶、控制與點雲配準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Targets, control and point-cloud registration\", which statement holds?","options":["偏差圖大部分是綠色，就代表竣工品質合格。","兩期點雲直接相減，就能偵測到小於單點雜訊的變形。","20 站以點雲匹配串聯，每一連接隨機誤差 2 mm，鏈末端累積約 √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm。"],"optionsEn":["If the deviation map is mostly green, the as-built quality is acceptable.","Subtracting two point clouds directly detects deformation smaller than single-point noise.","Chaining 20 stations by cloud matching with 2 mm random error per link accumulates about √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm at the end of the chain."],"answer":2,"explanation":"20 站以點雲匹配串聯，每一連接隨機誤差 2 mm，鏈末端累積約 √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm；若每 5 站以全測站控制標靶約束一次，累積僅約 √5×2 ≈ 4.5 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Chaining 20 stations by cloud matching with 2 mm random error per link accumulates about √20×2 ≈ 8.9 mm at the end of the chain; constraining every fifth station with total-station control targets limits accumulation to about √5×2 ≈ 4.5 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b098-v13-15","title":"標靶、控制與點雲配準：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Targets, control and point-cloud registration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「球形標靶與控制點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sphere targets and control points” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"配準報告須列出每個標靶與重疊區的殘差、整體平差統計與檢核標靶的偏差；檢核標靶由全測站獨立量測，偏差超過規格（例如 2σ 超出要求的 LOA 上限）時，該區點雲不得用於判定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The registration report must list residuals for each target and overlap, overall adjustment statistics and deviations at check targets; check targets are measured independently by total station, and if their deviations exceed the specification, for example a 2σ beyond the required LOA bound, that part of the cloud may not be used for conformance decisions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：規定每個掃描區至少有三個由全測站量測的控制標靶，另保留至少兩個檢核標靶；點雲一律以工地控制定位，不得先以最佳擬合對齊設計模型再做偏差分析。","observationEn":"Site practice: Require at least three total-station control targets for each scan area plus at least two check targets; always position clouds on site control and never best-fit them to the design model before deviation analysis.","failure":"注意干擾：長走廊只靠點雲自動匹配而沒有控制標靶，點雲沿長軸慢慢伸縮與彎曲，偏差圖顯示遠端牆面偏移數公分而被誤判為施工錯誤；或者整片點雲以最佳擬合對到設計模型，真實的整體偏移被抹去。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A long corridor registered only by automatic cloud matching, with no control targets, slowly stretches and bends along its axis, and the deviation map shows the far walls several centimetres out, wrongly blamed on construction; or the whole cloud is best-fitted to the design model and a real overall offset is erased. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"配準報告須列出每個標靶與重疊區的殘差、整體平差統計與檢核標靶的偏差；檢核標靶由全測站獨立量測，偏差超過規格（例如 2σ 超出要求的 LOA 上限）時，該區點雲不得用於判定。","textEn":"The registration report must list residuals for each target and overlap, overall adjustment statistics and deviations at check targets; check targets are measured independently by total station, and if their deviations exceed the specification, for example a 2σ beyond the required LOA bound, that part of the cloud may not be used for conformance decisions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"規定每個掃描區至少有三個由全測站量測的控制標靶，另保留至少兩個檢核標靶；點雲一律以工地控制定位，不得先以最佳擬合對齊設計模型再做偏差分析。","textEn":"Require at least three total-station control targets for each scan area plus at least two check targets; always position clouds on site control and never best-fit them to the design model before deviation analysis.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「標靶、控制與點雲配準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Targets, control and point-cloud registration\"?","options":["配準報告須列出每個標靶與重疊區的殘差、整體平差統計與檢核標靶的偏差。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","點雲有數百萬個點，所以每一點都比全測站量測更準確。"],"optionsEn":["The registration report must list residuals for each target and overlap, overall adjustment statistics and deviations at check targets.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A point cloud has millions of points, so every point is more accurate than a total-station measurement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"配準報告須列出每個標靶與重疊區的殘差、整體平差統計與檢核標靶的偏差；檢核標靶由全測站獨立量測，偏差超過規格（例如 2σ 超出要求的 LOA 上限）時，該區點雲不得用於判定。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The registration report must list residuals for each target and overlap, overall adjustment statistics and deviations at check targets; check targets are measured independently by total station, and if their deviations exceed the specification, for example a 2σ beyond the required LOA bound, that part of the cloud may not be used for conformance decisions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b098-v13-16","title":"標靶、控制與點雲配準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Targets, control and point-cloud registration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「球形標靶與控制點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sphere targets and control points” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"長走廊只靠點雲自動匹配而沒有控制標靶，點雲沿長軸慢慢伸縮與彎曲，偏差圖顯示遠端牆面偏移數公分而被誤判為施工錯誤；或者整片點雲以最佳擬合對到設計模型，真實的整體偏移被抹去。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A long corridor registered only by automatic cloud matching, with no control targets, slowly stretches and bends along its axis, and the deviation map shows the far walls several centimetres out, wrongly blamed on construction; or the whole cloud is best-fitted to the design model and a real overall offset is erased. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以全測站測得的控制標靶把點雲綁到工地控制網，並保留不參與配準的檢核標靶，才能證明配準結果可信。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Tying the cloud to the site control network through targets surveyed by total station, and keeping check targets that take no part in registration, is what proves the registration trustworthy.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「自動配準軟體顯示誤差很小，點雲位置就一定正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If automatic registration reports small errors, the cloud must be correctly positioned.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"長走廊只靠點雲自動匹配而沒有控制標靶，點雲沿長軸慢慢伸縮與彎曲，偏差圖顯示遠端牆面偏移數公分而被誤判為施工錯誤；或者整片點雲以最佳擬合對到設計模型，真實的整體偏移被抹去。","textEn":"A long corridor registered only by automatic cloud matching, with no control targets, slowly stretches and bends along its axis, and the deviation map shows the far walls several centimetres out, wrongly blamed on construction; or the whole cloud is best-fitted to the design model and a real overall offset is erased.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「標靶、控制與點雲配準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Targets, control and point-cloud registration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","長走廊只靠點雲自動匹配而沒有控制標靶，點雲沿長軸慢慢伸縮與彎曲，偏差圖顯示遠端牆面偏移數公分而被誤判為施工錯誤。","竣工掃描可以等全部完工後一次做完就好。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A long corridor registered only by automatic cloud matching, with no control targets, slowly stretches and bends along its axis, and the deviation map shows the far walls several centimetres out, wrongly blamed on construction.","As-built scanning can wait until everything is finished and be done once."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長走廊只靠點雲自動匹配而沒有控制標靶，點雲沿長軸慢慢伸縮與彎曲，偏差圖顯示遠端牆面偏移數公分而被誤判為施工錯誤；或者整片點雲以最佳擬合對到設計模型，真實的整體偏移被抹去。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A long corridor registered only by automatic cloud matching, with no control targets, slowly stretches and bends along its axis, and the deviation map shows the far walls several centimetres out, wrongly blamed on construction; or the whole cloud is best-fitted to the design model and a real overall offset is erased. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b098-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「依施工節點排定掃描」與「混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Scheduling scans at construction milestones\" and \"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b098-v13-17","title":"依施工節點排定掃描：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Scheduling scans at construction milestones: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「隱蔽前掃描時點」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pre-concealment scan window” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"竣工掃描最有價值的時點，是某些東西即將被蓋住或被下一工序依賴之前：澆置前的預埋件與套管、鋼構吊裝完成而帷幕牆托架尚未安裝、天花板封板前的機電管線、樓板澆置後的平整度。錯過時點就只能破壞檢查或接受不確定。掃描也受工地條件限制，人員與材料造成遮蔽、機具震動、粉塵與日照都有影響，所以掃描要像混凝土澆置一樣排進施工計畫，並保留清場時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隱蔽前掃描時點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The most valuable moments for as-built scanning come just before something is covered or relied on by the next trade: embeds and sleeves before a pour, steel after erection but before façade brackets go on, services before ceilings close, and slab flatness after a pour. Missing the moment leaves only destructive checks or accepted uncertainty. Scanning is also constrained by site conditions such as occlusion by people and materials, plant vibration, dust and sunlight, so scans belong in the construction programme like a concrete pour, with time reserved to clear the area. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Pre-concealment scan window” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：一個 2,000 m² 樓層，每站有效涵蓋約 150 m²（扣除遮蔽），需 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3，取 14 站；每站掃描 6 分鐘、移站 3 分鐘，共 14×9 = 126 分鐘 ≈ 2.1 小時，加上標靶布設與量測約 30 分鐘，每層約需 2.6 小時的清場窗口。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a 2,000 m² floor where each station effectively covers about 150 m² after occlusion, 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3, so 14 stations are needed; at 6 minutes scanning and 3 minutes moving per station that is 14×9 = 126 minutes ≈ 2.1 hours, plus about 30 minutes to place and survey targets, so each floor needs a cleared window of about 2.6 hours.","failure":"常見誤解：「竣工掃描可以等全部完工後一次做完就好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As-built scanning can wait until everything is finished and be done once.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隱蔽前掃描時點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Pre-concealment scan window”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-17-k1","title":"依施工節點排定掃描","titleEn":"Scheduling scans at construction milestones","text":"竣工掃描最有價值的時點，是某些東西即將被蓋住或被下一工序依賴之前：澆置前的預埋件與套管、鋼構吊裝完成而帷幕牆托架尚未安裝、天花板封板前的機電管線、樓板澆置後的平整度。錯過時點就只能破壞檢查或接受不確定。","textEn":"The most valuable moments for as-built scanning come just before something is covered or relied on by the next trade: embeds and sleeves before a pour, steel after erection but before façade brackets go on, services before ceilings close, and slab flatness after a pour. Missing the moment leaves only destructive checks or accepted uncertainty.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：竣工掃描可以等全部完工後一次做完就好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As-built scanning can wait until everything is finished and be done once. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「依施工節點排定掃描」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scheduling scans at construction milestones\" is correct?","options":["竣工掃描可以等全部完工後一次做完就好。","樓板澆置完成後形狀就固定不變，何時量測都一樣。","竣工掃描最有價值的時點，是某些東西即將被蓋住或被下一工序依賴之前：澆置前的預埋件與套管、鋼構吊裝完成而帷幕牆托架尚未安裝、天花板封板前的機電管線、樓板澆置後的平整度。"],"optionsEn":["As-built scanning can wait until everything is finished and be done once.","Once a slab is poured its shape is fixed, so it does not matter when it is measured.","The most valuable moments for as-built scanning come just before something is covered or relied on by the next trade: embeds and sleeves before a pour, steel after erection but before façade brackets go on, services before ceilings close, and slab flatness after a pour."],"answer":2,"explanation":"竣工掃描最有價值的時點，是某些東西即將被蓋住或被下一工序依賴之前：澆置前的預埋件與套管、鋼構吊裝完成而帷幕牆托架尚未安裝、天花板封板前的機電管線、樓板澆置後的平整度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The most valuable moments for as-built scanning come just before something is covered or relied on by the next trade: embeds and sleeves before a pour, steel after erection but before façade brackets go on, services before ceilings close, and slab flatness after a pour. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b098-v13-18","title":"依施工節點排定掃描：定量估算","titleEn":"Scheduling scans at construction milestones: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隱蔽前掃描時點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pre-concealment scan window” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：一個 2,000 m² 樓層，每站有效涵蓋約 150 m²（扣除遮蔽），需 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3，取 14 站；每站掃描 6 分鐘、移站 3 分鐘，共 14×9 = 126 分鐘 ≈ 2.1 小時，加上標靶布設與量測約 30 分鐘，每層約需 2.6 小時的清場窗口。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a 2,000 m² floor where each station effectively covers about 150 m² after occlusion, 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3, so 14 stations are needed; at 6 minutes scanning and 3 minutes moving per station that is 14×9 = 126 minutes ≈ 2.1 hours, plus about 30 minutes to place and survey targets, so each floor needs a cleared window of about 2.6 hours. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把掃描節點寫入施工排程並設為檢查點，由監造確認掃描已完成、資料初步檢查無缺漏後，才允許澆置、封板或安裝下一工序；每次掃描記錄天候、溫度、遮蔽與現場狀況，供日後解讀偏差時參考。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Write scan milestones into the programme as inspection points, allowing a pour, close-up or next installation only after the supervising engineer confirms the scan is done and a first check shows no gaps; record weather, temperature, occlusion and site conditions at each scan to help interpret deviations later.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"一個 2,000 m² 樓層，每站有效涵蓋約 150 m²（扣除遮蔽），需 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3，取 14 站；每站掃描 6 分鐘、移站 3 分鐘，共 14×9 = 126 分鐘 ≈ 2.1 小時，加上標靶布設與量測約 30 分鐘，每層約需 2.6 小時的清場窗口。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a 2,000 m² floor where each station effectively covers about 150 m² after occlusion, 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3, so 14 stations are needed; at 6 minutes scanning and 3 minutes moving per station that is 14×9 = 126 minutes ≈ 2.1 hours, plus about 30 minutes to place and survey targets, so each floor needs a cleared window of about 2.6 hours. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「依施工節點排定掃描」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scheduling scans at construction milestones\", which statement holds?","options":["一個 2,000 m² 樓層，每站有效涵蓋約 150 m²（扣除遮蔽），需 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3，取 14 站。","配準軟體報告的誤差就是點雲的絕對精度。","點雲交出檔案就完成交接，不需要後設資料。"],"optionsEn":["For a 2,000 m² floor where each station effectively covers about 150 m² after occlusion, 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3, so 14 stations are needed.","The error reported by registration software is the absolute accuracy of the cloud.","Handing over the point-cloud files completes the handover; metadata is unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一個 2,000 m² 樓層，每站有效涵蓋約 150 m²（扣除遮蔽），需 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3，取 14 站；每站掃描 6 分鐘、移站 3 分鐘，共 14×9 = 126 分鐘 ≈ 2.1 小時，加上標靶布設與量測約 30 分鐘，每層約需 2.6 小時的清場窗口。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a 2,000 m² floor where each station effectively covers about 150 m² after occlusion, 2,000/150 ≈ 13.3, so 14 stations are needed; at 6 minutes scanning and 3 minutes moving per station that is 14×9 = 126 minutes ≈ 2.1 hours, plus about 30 minutes to place and survey targets, so each floor needs a cleared window of about 2.6 hours. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b098-v13-19","title":"依施工節點排定掃描：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scheduling scans at construction milestones: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隱蔽前掃描時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pre-concealment scan window” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把掃描節點寫入施工排程並設為檢查點，由監造確認掃描已完成、資料初步檢查無缺漏後，才允許澆置、封板或安裝下一工序；每次掃描記錄天候、溫度、遮蔽與現場狀況，供日後解讀偏差時參考。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Write scan milestones into the programme as inspection points, allowing a pour, close-up or next installation only after the supervising engineer confirms the scan is done and a first check shows no gaps; record weather, temperature, occlusion and site conditions at each scan to help interpret deviations later. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在施工計畫中列出掃描節點清單（預埋件、鋼構、機電封板前、樓板平整度、帷幕牆托架），每個節點都是保留點，未經監造確認不得進入下一工序。","observationEn":"Site practice: List scan milestones in the construction plan (embeds, steelwork, services before close-up, slab flatness, façade brackets), make each a hold point, and do not proceed to the next trade without the supervising engineer's confirmation.","failure":"注意干擾：天花板封板趕在掃描之前完成，機電竣工位置只能依施工圖推定；多年後維修人員找閥門與管線時發現與模型差了數十公分，只好逐片拆天花板查找。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ceilings closed before the scan leave the as-built services positions to be inferred from shop drawings; years later maintenance staff looking for valves and pipes find them tens of centimetres from the model and have to remove ceiling tiles one by one. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把掃描節點寫入施工排程並設為檢查點，由監造確認掃描已完成、資料初步檢查無缺漏後，才允許澆置、封板或安裝下一工序；每次掃描記錄天候、溫度、遮蔽與現場狀況，供日後解讀偏差時參考。","textEn":"Write scan milestones into the programme as inspection points, allowing a pour, close-up or next installation only after the supervising engineer confirms the scan is done and a first check shows no gaps; record weather, temperature, occlusion and site conditions at each scan to help interpret deviations later.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在施工計畫中列出掃描節點清單（預埋件、鋼構、機電封板前、樓板平整度、帷幕牆托架），每個節點都是保留點，未經監造確認不得進入下一工序。","textEn":"List scan milestones in the construction plan (embeds, steelwork, services before close-up, slab flatness, façade brackets), make each a hold point, and do not proceed to the next trade without the supervising engineer's confirmation.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「依施工節點排定掃描」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scheduling scans at construction milestones\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","把掃描節點寫入施工排程並設為檢查點，由監造確認掃描已完成、資料初步檢查無缺漏後，才允許澆置、封板或安裝下一工序。","點雲精度很高，由它建立的模型自然也同樣精確。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Write scan milestones into the programme as inspection points, allowing a pour, close-up or next installation only after the supervising engineer confirms the scan is done and a first check shows no gaps.","If the point cloud is accurate, the model built from it is automatically just as accurate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把掃描節點寫入施工排程並設為檢查點，由監造確認掃描已完成、資料初步檢查無缺漏後，才允許澆置、封板或安裝下一工序；每次掃描記錄天候、溫度、遮蔽與現場狀況，供日後解讀偏差時參考。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Write scan milestones into the programme as inspection points, allowing a pour, close-up or next installation only after the supervising engineer confirms the scan is done and a first check shows no gaps; record weather, temperature, occlusion and site conditions at each scan to help interpret deviations later. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b098-v13-20","title":"依施工節點排定掃描：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scheduling scans at construction milestones: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隱蔽前掃描時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pre-concealment scan window” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"天花板封板趕在掃描之前完成，機電竣工位置只能依施工圖推定；多年後維修人員找閥門與管線時發現與模型差了數十公分，只好逐片拆天花板查找。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ceilings closed before the scan leave the as-built services positions to be inferred from shop drawings; years later maintenance staff looking for valves and pipes find them tens of centimetres from the model and have to remove ceiling tiles one by one. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：掃描也受工地條件限制，人員與材料造成遮蔽、機具震動、粉塵與日照都有影響，所以掃描要像混凝土澆置一樣排進施工計畫，並保留清場時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Scanning is also constrained by site conditions such as occlusion by people and materials, plant vibration, dust and sunlight, so scans belong in the construction programme like a concrete pour, with time reserved to clear the area.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「竣工掃描可以等全部完工後一次做完就好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As-built scanning can wait until everything is finished and be done once.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"天花板封板趕在掃描之前完成，機電竣工位置只能依施工圖推定；多年後維修人員找閥門與管線時發現與模型差了數十公分，只好逐片拆天花板查找。","textEn":"Ceilings closed before the scan leave the as-built services positions to be inferred from shop drawings; years later maintenance staff looking for valves and pipes find them tens of centimetres from the model and have to remove ceiling tiles one by one.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「依施工節點排定掃描」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scheduling scans at construction milestones\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","樓板澆置完成後形狀就固定不變，何時量測都一樣。","天花板封板趕在掃描之前完成，機電竣工位置只能依施工圖推定；多年後維修人員找閥門與管線時發現與模型差了數十公分，只好逐片拆天花板查找。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Once a slab is poured its shape is fixed, so it does not matter when it is measured.","Ceilings closed before the scan leave the as-built services positions to be inferred from shop drawings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"天花板封板趕在掃描之前完成，機電竣工位置只能依施工圖推定；多年後維修人員找閥門與管線時發現與模型差了數十公分，只好逐片拆天花板查找。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ceilings closed before the scan leave the as-built services positions to be inferred from shop drawings; years later maintenance staff looking for valves and pipes find them tens of centimetres from the model and have to remove ceiling tiles one by one. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b098-v13-21","title":"混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「樓板高程色階圖」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Slab elevation heat map” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"樓板的平整度與水平度影響架高地板、倉儲貨架、帷幕牆底部收邊與地坪材料厚度。傳統以水準儀在格點量測，或依 ASTM E1155 沿量測線計算 F 數；雷射掃描能一次取得整片樓板的高程，畫成色階圖顯示高點與低點，並據以估算研磨量或自平材料用量。混凝土澆置後還會因乾縮翹曲與撤撐後的撓度改變形狀，所以量測時點必須與規格約定的時點一致。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「樓板高程色階圖」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Slab flatness and levelness affect raised floors, warehouse racking, the bottom closure of curtain walls and the thickness of floor finishes. Traditionally a level is read at grid points, or F-numbers are computed along survey lines to ASTM E1155; laser scanning captures the elevation of the whole slab at once and plots it as a heat map of highs and lows from which grinding or self-levelling quantities are estimated. After pouring, concrete changes shape through shrinkage curling and deflection when shoring is removed, so the time of measurement must match the time the specification refers to. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Slab elevation heat map” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：400 m² 的低窪區平均比設計高程低 6 mm，所需自平材料約 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 400 m² low area averaging 6 mm below design level needs about 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³ of self-levelling compound.","failure":"常見誤解：「樓板澆置完成後形狀就固定不變，何時量測都一樣。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once a slab is poured its shape is fixed, so it does not matter when it is measured.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「樓板高程色階圖」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Slab elevation heat map”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-21-k1","title":"混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗","titleEn":"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness","text":"樓板的平整度與水平度影響架高地板、倉儲貨架、帷幕牆底部收邊與地坪材料厚度。傳統以水準儀在格點量測，或依 ASTM E1155 沿量測線計算 F 數；雷射掃描能一次取得整片樓板的高程，畫成色階圖顯示高點與低點，並據以估算研磨量或自平材料用量。","textEn":"Slab flatness and levelness affect raised floors, warehouse racking, the bottom closure of curtain walls and the thickness of floor finishes. Traditionally a level is read at grid points, or F-numbers are computed along survey lines to ASTM E1155; laser scanning captures the elevation of the whole slab at once and plots it as a heat map of highs and lows from which grinding or self-levelling quantities are estimated.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：樓板澆置完成後形狀就固定不變，何時量測都一樣。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once a slab is poured its shape is fixed, so it does not matter when it is measured. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness\" is correct?","options":["樓板的平整度與水平度影響架高地板、倉儲貨架、帷幕牆底部收邊與地坪材料厚度。","樓板澆置完成後形狀就固定不變，何時量測都一樣。","偏差圖大部分是綠色，就代表竣工品質合格。"],"optionsEn":["Slab flatness and levelness affect raised floors, warehouse racking, the bottom closure of curtain walls and the thickness of floor finishes.","Once a slab is poured its shape is fixed, so it does not matter when it is measured.","If the deviation map is mostly green, the as-built quality is acceptable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"樓板的平整度與水平度影響架高地板、倉儲貨架、帷幕牆底部收邊與地坪材料厚度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Slab flatness and levelness affect raised floors, warehouse racking, the bottom closure of curtain walls and the thickness of floor finishes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b098-v13-22","title":"混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樓板高程色階圖」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Slab elevation heat map” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：400 m² 的低窪區平均比設計高程低 6 mm，所需自平材料約 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³。兩個相距 3 m 的點高差 8 mm，坡度 8/3,000 ≈ 1/375；若規格要求 3 m 內高差不超過 5 mm，該處需研磨或補平。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 400 m² low area averaging 6 mm below design level needs about 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³ of self-levelling compound. Two points 3 m apart differing by 8 mm give a slope of 8/3,000 ≈ 1/375; if the specification allows no more than 5 mm over 3 m, that location needs grinding or filling. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依規格約定的時點掃描（例如澆置後固定天數內，或撤撐前後各一次），以控制點將點雲定位到設計高程，再以格點與量測線抽取高程，與水準儀抽驗點比較；計算結果與色階圖一起提交監造審查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Scan at the time the specification agrees, for example within a fixed number of days after the pour or before and after shoring removal, position the cloud to design levels through control points, extract elevations at grid points and survey lines, and compare them with spot checks by level; submit the results with the heat map for the supervising engineer's review.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"400 m² 的低窪區平均比設計高程低 6 mm，所需自平材料約 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³。兩個相距 3 m 的點高差 8 mm，坡度 8/3,000 ≈ 1/375；若規格要求 3 m 內高差不超過 5 mm，該處需研磨或補平。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A 400 m² low area averaging 6 mm below design level needs about 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³ of self-levelling compound. Two points 3 m apart differing by 8 mm give a slope of 8/3,000 ≈ 1/375; if the specification allows no more than 5 mm over 3 m, that location needs grinding or filling. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness\", which statement holds?","options":["兩期點雲直接相減，就能偵測到小於單點雜訊的變形。","400 m² 的低窪區平均比設計高程低 6 mm，所需自平材料約 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³。","點雲有數百萬個點，所以每一點都比全測站量測更準確。"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting two point clouds directly detects deformation smaller than single-point noise.","A 400 m² low area averaging 6 mm below design level needs about 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³ of self-levelling compound.","A point cloud has millions of points, so every point is more accurate than a total-station measurement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"400 m² 的低窪區平均比設計高程低 6 mm，所需自平材料約 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 400 m² low area averaging 6 mm below design level needs about 400×0.006 = 2.4 m³ of self-levelling compound. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b098-v13-23","title":"混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樓板高程色階圖」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Slab elevation heat map” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依規格約定的時點掃描（例如澆置後固定天數內，或撤撐前後各一次），以控制點將點雲定位到設計高程，再以格點與量測線抽取高程，與水準儀抽驗點比較；計算結果與色階圖一起提交監造審查。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Scan at the time the specification agrees, for example within a fixed number of days after the pour or before and after shoring removal, position the cloud to design levels through control points, extract elevations at grid points and survey lines, and compare them with spot checks by level; submit the results with the heat map for the supervising engineer's review. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：規格要同時寫明平整度指標、量測方法、量測時點與基準高程，並把撤撐前的掃描列為保留點；需研磨或補平的範圍經監造確認後才可施作面層。","observationEn":"Site practice: The specification must state the flatness measure, measurement method, measurement time and reference level together, with a pre-shoring-removal scan as a hold point; areas needing grinding or filling are confirmed by the supervising engineer before finishes are laid.","failure":"注意干擾：撤撐後才掃描並據以判定施工不合格，承包商主張偏差來自結構撓度而非澆置，雙方各執一詞；若量測時點未在合約中約定，爭議只能靠第三方鑑定解決。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Scanning only after shoring removal and judging the pour nonconforming leads the contractor to argue that the deviation is structural deflection rather than placement; if the measurement time was never agreed in the contract, the dispute can only be settled by third-party appraisal. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依規格約定的時點掃描（例如澆置後固定天數內，或撤撐前後各一次），以控制點將點雲定位到設計高程，再以格點與量測線抽取高程，與水準儀抽驗點比較；計算結果與色階圖一起提交監造審查。","textEn":"Scan at the time the specification agrees, for example within a fixed number of days after the pour or before and after shoring removal, position the cloud to design levels through control points, extract elevations at grid points and survey lines, and compare them with spot checks by level; submit the results with the heat map for the supervising engineer's review.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"規格要同時寫明平整度指標、量測方法、量測時點與基準高程，並把撤撐前的掃描列為保留點；需研磨或補平的範圍經監造確認後才可施作面層。","textEn":"The specification must state the flatness measure, measurement method, measurement time and reference level together, with a pre-shoring-removal scan as a hold point; areas needing grinding or filling are confirmed by the supervising engineer before finishes are laid.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","掃描儀的標稱精度在任何距離與角度都一樣。","依規格約定的時點掃描（例如澆置後固定天數內，或撤撐前後各一次），以控制點將點雲定位到設計高程，再以格點與量測線抽取高程，與水準儀抽驗點比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A scanner's nominal accuracy holds at every range and angle.","Scan at the time the specification agrees, for example within a fixed number of days after the pour or before and after shoring removal, position the cloud to design levels through control points, extract elevations at grid points and survey lines, and compare them with spot checks by level."],"answer":2,"explanation":"依規格約定的時點掃描（例如澆置後固定天數內，或撤撐前後各一次），以控制點將點雲定位到設計高程，再以格點與量測線抽取高程，與水準儀抽驗點比較；計算結果與色階圖一起提交監造審查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Scan at the time the specification agrees, for example within a fixed number of days after the pour or before and after shoring removal, position the cloud to design levels through control points, extract elevations at grid points and survey lines, and compare them with spot checks by level; submit the results with the heat map for the supervising engineer's review. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b098-v13-24","title":"混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樓板高程色階圖」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Slab elevation heat map” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"撤撐後才掃描並據以判定施工不合格，承包商主張偏差來自結構撓度而非澆置，雙方各執一詞；若量測時點未在合約中約定，爭議只能靠第三方鑑定解決。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Scanning only after shoring removal and judging the pour nonconforming leads the contractor to argue that the deviation is structural deflection rather than placement; if the measurement time was never agreed in the contract, the dispute can only be settled by third-party appraisal. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：混凝土澆置後還會因乾縮翹曲與撤撐後的撓度改變形狀，所以量測時點必須與規格約定的時點一致。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: After pouring, concrete changes shape through shrinkage curling and deflection when shoring is removed, so the time of measurement must match the time the specification refers to.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「樓板澆置完成後形狀就固定不變，何時量測都一樣。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once a slab is poured its shape is fixed, so it does not matter when it is measured.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"撤撐後才掃描並據以判定施工不合格，承包商主張偏差來自結構撓度而非澆置，雙方各執一詞；若量測時點未在合約中約定，爭議只能靠第三方鑑定解決。","textEn":"Scanning only after shoring removal and judging the pour nonconforming leads the contractor to argue that the deviation is structural deflection rather than placement; if the measurement time was never agreed in the contract, the dispute can only be settled by third-party appraisal.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「混凝土樓板平整度的掃描檢驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scan-based checks of slab flatness and levelness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["撤撐後才掃描並據以判定施工不合格，承包商主張偏差來自結構撓度而非澆置，雙方各執一詞；若量測時點未在合約中約定，爭議只能靠第三方鑑定解決。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","偏差圖大部分是綠色，就代表竣工品質合格。"],"optionsEn":["Scanning only after shoring removal and judging the pour nonconforming leads the contractor to argue that the deviation is structural deflection rather than placement.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If the deviation map is mostly green, the as-built quality is acceptable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"撤撐後才掃描並據以判定施工不合格，承包商主張偏差來自結構撓度而非澆置，雙方各執一詞；若量測時點未在合約中約定，爭議只能靠第三方鑑定解決。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Scanning only after shoring removal and judging the pour nonconforming leads the contractor to argue that the deviation is structural deflection rather than placement; if the measurement time was never agreed in the contract, the dispute can only be settled by third-party appraisal. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b098-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「點雲與設計模型的偏差分析」與「掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model\" and \"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b098-v13-25","title":"點雲與設計模型的偏差分析：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「點雲與模型偏差圖」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cloud-to-model deviation map” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"偏差分析計算每個點到設計模型表面的距離，再依元素統計平均值、標準差與落在公差內的比例，並以色階圖呈現。結果強烈依賴對齊方式：以控制網定位時，系統性偏移會如實呈現；若把點雲最佳擬合到模型，整體偏移被吸收，看起來幾乎全部合格。因此偏差分析要同時檢視平均偏移與離散程度，並逐一元素呈現，而非整棟建築一個數字。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「點雲與模型偏差圖」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Deviation analysis computes the distance from each point to the design-model surface, then reports mean, standard deviation and the share within tolerance for each element, displayed as a colour map. Results depend strongly on alignment: positioning on the control network shows systematic offsets as they are, while best-fitting the cloud to the model absorbs the overall offset and makes nearly everything look compliant. Deviation analysis must therefore examine mean offset and scatter together, element by element rather than as one number for the building. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Cloud-to-model deviation map” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：牆面偏差以控制定位時平均 +7 mm、標準差 4 mm，落在 ±10 mm 內的比例 = Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773，約 77%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With control-based positioning a wall shows mean deviation +7 mm and standard deviation 4 mm, so the share within ±10 mm is Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773, about 77%.","failure":"常見誤解：「偏差圖大部分是綠色，就代表竣工品質合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the deviation map is mostly green, the as-built quality is acceptable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「點雲與模型偏差圖」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Cloud-to-model deviation map”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-25-k1","title":"點雲與設計模型的偏差分析","titleEn":"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model","text":"偏差分析計算每個點到設計模型表面的距離，再依元素統計平均值、標準差與落在公差內的比例，並以色階圖呈現。結果強烈依賴對齊方式：以控制網定位時，系統性偏移會如實呈現；若把點雲最佳擬合到模型，整體偏移被吸收，看起來幾乎全部合格。","textEn":"Deviation analysis computes the distance from each point to the design-model surface, then reports mean, standard deviation and the share within tolerance for each element, displayed as a colour map. Results depend strongly on alignment: positioning on the control network shows systematic offsets as they are, while best-fitting the cloud to the model absorbs the overall offset and makes nearly everything look compliant.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：偏差圖大部分是綠色，就代表竣工品質合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the deviation map is mostly green, the as-built quality is acceptable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「點雲與設計模型的偏差分析」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model\" is correct?","options":["偏差圖大部分是綠色，就代表竣工品質合格。","偏差分析計算每個點到設計模型表面的距離，再依元素統計平均值、標準差與落在公差內的比例，並以色階圖呈現。","配準軟體報告的誤差就是點雲的絕對精度。"],"optionsEn":["If the deviation map is mostly green, the as-built quality is acceptable.","Deviation analysis computes the distance from each point to the design-model surface, then reports mean, standard deviation and the share within tolerance for each element, displayed as a colour map.","The error reported by registration software is the absolute accuracy of the cloud."],"answer":1,"explanation":"偏差分析計算每個點到設計模型表面的距離，再依元素統計平均值、標準差與落在公差內的比例，並以色階圖呈現。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Deviation analysis computes the distance from each point to the design-model surface, then reports mean, standard deviation and the share within tolerance for each element, displayed as a colour map. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b098-v13-26","title":"點雲與設計模型的偏差分析：定量估算","titleEn":"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「點雲與模型偏差圖」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cloud-to-model deviation map” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：牆面偏差以控制定位時平均 +7 mm、標準差 4 mm，落在 ±10 mm 內的比例 = Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773，約 77%。若以最佳擬合使平均變為 0，比例 = Φ(2.5) − Φ(−2.5) ≈ 0.988，看似 99% 合格，但 7 mm 的系統偏移被隱藏。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With control-based positioning a wall shows mean deviation +7 mm and standard deviation 4 mm, so the share within ±10 mm is Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773, about 77%. Best-fitting to zero mean gives Φ(2.5) − Φ(−2.5) ≈ 0.988, apparently 99% compliant, while the 7 mm systematic offset is hidden. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：偏差報告要說明對齊方式與控制來源，逐元素列出平均偏移、標準差、最大偏差與合格比例，並附色階圖與剖面；偏差集中的區域以全測站或捲尺抽驗確認，再交由設計者判斷是否影響下一工序。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The deviation report must state the alignment method and control source, list mean offset, standard deviation, maximum deviation and compliant share element by element with colour maps and sections, spot-check areas of concentrated deviation by total station or tape, and pass them to the designer to judge the effect on the next trade.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"牆面偏差以控制定位時平均 +7 mm、標準差 4 mm，落在 ±10 mm 內的比例 = Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773，約 77%。若以最佳擬合使平均變為 0，比例 = Φ(2.5) − Φ(−2.5) ≈ 0.988，看似 99% 合格，但 7 mm 的系統偏移被隱藏。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With control-based positioning a wall shows mean deviation +7 mm and standard deviation 4 mm, so the share within ±10 mm is Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773, about 77%. Best-fitting to zero mean gives Φ(2.5) − Φ(−2.5) ≈ 0.988, apparently 99% compliant, while the 7 mm systematic offset is hidden. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「點雲與設計模型的偏差分析」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model\", which statement holds?","options":["點雲交出檔案就完成交接，不需要後設資料。","點雲精度很高，由它建立的模型自然也同樣精確。","牆面偏差以控制定位時平均 +7 mm、標準差 4 mm，落在 ±10 mm 內的比例 = Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773，約 77%。"],"optionsEn":["Handing over the point-cloud files completes the handover; metadata is unnecessary.","If the point cloud is accurate, the model built from it is automatically just as accurate.","With control-based positioning a wall shows mean deviation +7 mm and standard deviation 4 mm, so the share within ±10 mm is Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773, about 77%."],"answer":2,"explanation":"牆面偏差以控制定位時平均 +7 mm、標準差 4 mm，落在 ±10 mm 內的比例 = Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773，約 77%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With control-based positioning a wall shows mean deviation +7 mm and standard deviation 4 mm, so the share within ±10 mm is Φ((10−7)/4) − Φ((−10−7)/4) = Φ(0.75) − Φ(−4.25) ≈ 0.773, about 77%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b098-v13-27","title":"點雲與設計模型的偏差分析：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「點雲與模型偏差圖」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cloud-to-model deviation map” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"偏差報告要說明對齊方式與控制來源，逐元素列出平均偏移、標準差、最大偏差與合格比例，並附色階圖與剖面；偏差集中的區域以全測站或捲尺抽驗確認，再交由設計者判斷是否影響下一工序。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The deviation report must state the alignment method and control source, list mean offset, standard deviation, maximum deviation and compliant share element by element with colour maps and sections, spot-check areas of concentrated deviation by total station or tape, and pass them to the designer to judge the effect on the next trade. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：偏差分析一律以工地控制定位，禁止先最佳擬合再判定；報告須依元素類別與下一工序的介面位置分區呈現，並由設計者與下一工序承包商共同簽閱。","observationEn":"Site practice: Always position deviation analysis on site control and never best-fit before judging; present reports by element class and by interface zones with the next trade, signed by both the designer and the following contractor.","failure":"注意干擾：報告只給整棟樓「95% 點位在公差內」的單一數字，實際上 5% 的超差點全集中在帷幕牆托架所在的樓板邊緣，直到帷幕牆單元到場無法安裝才被發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A report giving a single building-wide figure of ‘95% of points within tolerance’ hides that the 5% outside are all at slab edges where façade brackets sit, so the problem appears only when curtain-wall units arrive and cannot be installed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"偏差報告要說明對齊方式與控制來源，逐元素列出平均偏移、標準差、最大偏差與合格比例，並附色階圖與剖面；偏差集中的區域以全測站或捲尺抽驗確認，再交由設計者判斷是否影響下一工序。","textEn":"The deviation report must state the alignment method and control source, list mean offset, standard deviation, maximum deviation and compliant share element by element with colour maps and sections, spot-check areas of concentrated deviation by total station or tape, and pass them to the designer to judge the effect on the next trade.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"偏差分析一律以工地控制定位，禁止先最佳擬合再判定；報告須依元素類別與下一工序的介面位置分區呈現，並由設計者與下一工序承包商共同簽閱。","textEn":"Always position deviation analysis on site control and never best-fit before judging; present reports by element class and by interface zones with the next trade, signed by both the designer and the following contractor.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「點雲與設計模型的偏差分析」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model\"?","options":["偏差報告要說明對齊方式與控制來源，逐元素列出平均偏移、標準差、最大偏差與合格比例，並附色階圖與剖面。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","自動配準軟體顯示誤差很小，點雲位置就一定正確。"],"optionsEn":["The deviation report must state the alignment method and control source, list mean offset, standard deviation, maximum deviation and compliant share element by element with colour maps and sections, spot-check areas of concentrated deviation by total station or tape, and pass them to the designer to judge the effect on the next trade.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If automatic registration reports small errors, the cloud must be correctly positioned."],"answer":0,"explanation":"偏差報告要說明對齊方式與控制來源，逐元素列出平均偏移、標準差、最大偏差與合格比例，並附色階圖與剖面；偏差集中的區域以全測站或捲尺抽驗確認，再交由設計者判斷是否影響下一工序。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The deviation report must state the alignment method and control source, list mean offset, standard deviation, maximum deviation and compliant share element by element with colour maps and sections, spot-check areas of concentrated deviation by total station or tape, and pass them to the designer to judge the effect on the next trade. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b098-v13-28","title":"點雲與設計模型的偏差分析：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「點雲與模型偏差圖」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cloud-to-model deviation map” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"報告只給整棟樓「95% 點位在公差內」的單一數字，實際上 5% 的超差點全集中在帷幕牆托架所在的樓板邊緣，直到帷幕牆單元到場無法安裝才被發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A report giving a single building-wide figure of ‘95% of points within tolerance’ hides that the 5% outside are all at slab edges where façade brackets sit, so the problem appears only when curtain-wall units arrive and cannot be installed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此偏差分析要同時檢視平均偏移與離散程度，並逐一元素呈現，而非整棟建築一個數字。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Deviation analysis must therefore examine mean offset and scatter together, element by element rather than as one number for the building.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「偏差圖大部分是綠色，就代表竣工品質合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the deviation map is mostly green, the as-built quality is acceptable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"報告只給整棟樓「95% 點位在公差內」的單一數字，實際上 5% 的超差點全集中在帷幕牆托架所在的樓板邊緣，直到帷幕牆單元到場無法安裝才被發現。","textEn":"A report giving a single building-wide figure of ‘95% of points within tolerance’ hides that the 5% outside are all at slab edges where façade brackets sit, so the problem appears only when curtain-wall units arrive and cannot be installed.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「點雲與設計模型的偏差分析」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deviation analysis between cloud and design model\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","報告只給整棟樓「95% 點位在公差內」的單一數字，實際上 5% 的超差點全集中在帷幕牆托架所在的樓板邊緣，直到帷幕牆單元到場無法安裝才被發現。","配準軟體報告的誤差就是點雲的絕對精度。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A report giving a single building-wide figure of ‘95% of points within tolerance’ hides that the 5% outside are all at slab edges where façade brackets sit, so the problem appears only when curtain-wall units arrive and cannot be installed.","The error reported by registration software is the absolute accuracy of the cloud."],"answer":1,"explanation":"報告只給整棟樓「95% 點位在公差內」的單一數字，實際上 5% 的超差點全集中在帷幕牆托架所在的樓板邊緣，直到帷幕牆單元到場無法安裝才被發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A report giving a single building-wide figure of ‘95% of points within tolerance’ hides that the 5% outside are all at slab edges where façade brackets sit, so the problem appears only when curtain-wall units arrive and cannot be installed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b098-v13-29","title":"掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「獨立檢核點」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Independent check points” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"掃描成果的精度不能只引用儀器規格或配準軟體的數字，而要以獨立檢核點證明：在掃描範圍內設置一批由全測站量測、未參與配準的檢核點，比較它們在點雲中的坐標與全測站坐標，計算均方根誤差。ISO 17123-9 規定以現場程序檢查地面雷射掃描儀的重複精度，可在專案開始前與定期檢查時使用；檢核結果再與 LOA 規格比較，決定成果能否用於判定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「獨立檢核點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The accuracy of a scan cannot simply be quoted from the instrument specification or the registration software; it must be shown with independent check points. A set of points surveyed by total station, not used in registration, is placed within the scanned area, and their cloud coordinates are compared with total-station coordinates to compute the root-mean-square error. ISO 17123-9 gives field procedures for checking the repeatability of terrestrial laser scanners, usable before a project and at periodic checks, and the check-point result is compared with the LOA specification to decide whether the data can support conformance decisions. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Independent check points” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：10 個檢核點的殘差（mm）為 2.1、−1.5、3.0、−2.4、1.2、0.8、−2.9、1.9、−0.6、2.6，平方和 = 42.64，RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm，2σ 約 4.1 mm，落在 1 至 5 mm 的等級範圍內但接近上限。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Ten check-point residuals (mm) of 2.1, −1.5, 3.0, −2.4, 1.2, 0.8, −2.9, 1.9, −0.6 and 2.6 give a sum of squares of 42.64 and RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm, a 2σ of about 4.1 mm, inside a 1 to 5 mm class but near its upper bound.","failure":"常見誤解：「配準軟體報告的誤差就是點雲的絕對精度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The error reported by registration software is the absolute accuracy of the cloud.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「獨立檢核點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Independent check points”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-29-k1","title":"掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定","titleEn":"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners","text":"掃描成果的精度不能只引用儀器規格或配準軟體的數字，而要以獨立檢核點證明：在掃描範圍內設置一批由全測站量測、未參與配準的檢核點，比較它們在點雲中的坐標與全測站坐標，計算均方根誤差。ISO 17123-9 規定以現場程序檢查地面雷射掃描儀的重複精度，可在專案開始前與定期檢查時使用；檢核結果再與 LOA 規格比較，決定成果能否用於判定。","textEn":"The accuracy of a scan cannot simply be quoted from the instrument specification or the registration software; it must be shown with independent check points. A set of points surveyed by total station, not used in registration, is placed within the scanned area, and their cloud coordinates are compared with total-station coordinates to compute the root-mean-square error.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：配準軟體報告的誤差就是點雲的絕對精度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The error reported by registration software is the absolute accuracy of the cloud. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners\" is correct?","options":["配準軟體報告的誤差就是點雲的絕對精度。","兩期點雲直接相減，就能偵測到小於單點雜訊的變形。","掃描成果的精度不能只引用儀器規格或配準軟體的數字，而要以獨立檢核點證明：在掃描範圍內設置一批由全測站量測、未參與配準的檢核點，比較它們在點雲中的坐標與全測站坐標，計算均方根誤差。"],"optionsEn":["The error reported by registration software is the absolute accuracy of the cloud.","Subtracting two point clouds directly detects deformation smaller than single-point noise.","The accuracy of a scan cannot simply be quoted from the instrument specification or the registration software; it must be shown with independent check points."],"answer":2,"explanation":"掃描成果的精度不能只引用儀器規格或配準軟體的數字，而要以獨立檢核點證明：在掃描範圍內設置一批由全測站量測、未參與配準的檢核點，比較它們在點雲中的坐標與全測站坐標，計算均方根誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The accuracy of a scan cannot simply be quoted from the instrument specification or the registration software; it must be shown with independent check points. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b098-v13-30","title":"掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定：定量估算","titleEn":"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「獨立檢核點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Independent check points” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：10 個檢核點的殘差（mm）為 2.1、−1.5、3.0、−2.4、1.2、0.8、−2.9、1.9、−0.6、2.6，平方和 = 42.64，RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm，2σ 約 4.1 mm，落在 1 至 5 mm 的等級範圍內但接近上限。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Ten check-point residuals (mm) of 2.1, −1.5, 3.0, −2.4, 1.2, 0.8, −2.9, 1.9, −0.6 and 2.6 give a sum of squares of 42.64 and RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm, a 2σ of about 4.1 mm, inside a 1 to 5 mm class but near its upper bound. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：檢核點應分布在掃描範圍四周與中央、不同高度與距離，數量依面積訂定；每台掃描儀在專案開始前依 ISO 17123-9 做現場檢定並保存紀錄，檢核點結果與 LOA 規格一起列入交付報告，未達規格者重掃或補控制。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Distribute check points around the edges and centre of the scanned area at different heights and ranges, with numbers set by area; test each scanner in the field to ISO 17123-9 before the project and keep the records, include check-point results with the LOA specification in the delivery report, and re-scan or add control where the specification is not met.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"10 個檢核點的殘差（mm）為 2.1、−1.5、3.0、−2.4、1.2、0.8、−2.9、1.9、−0.6、2.6，平方和 = 42.64，RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm，2σ 約 4.1 mm，落在 1 至 5 mm 的等級範圍內但接近上限。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Ten check-point residuals (mm) of 2.1, −1.5, 3.0, −2.4, 1.2, 0.8, −2.9, 1.9, −0.6 and 2.6 give a sum of squares of 42.64 and RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm, a 2σ of about 4.1 mm, inside a 1 to 5 mm class but near its upper bound. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners\", which statement holds?","options":["10 個檢核點的殘差（mm）為 2.1、−1.5、3.0、−2.4、1.2、0.8、−2.9、1.9、−0.6、2.6，平方和 = 42.64，RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm，2σ 約 4.1 mm，落在 1 至 5 mm 的等級範圍內但接近上限。","點雲有數百萬個點，所以每一點都比全測站量測更準確。","掃描儀的標稱精度在任何距離與角度都一樣。"],"optionsEn":["Ten check-point residuals (mm) of 2.1, −1.5, 3.0, −2.4, 1.2, 0.8, −2.9, 1.9, −0.6 and 2.6 give a sum of squares of 42.64 and RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm, a 2σ of about 4.1 mm, inside a 1 to 5 mm class but near its upper bound.","A point cloud has millions of points, so every point is more accurate than a total-station measurement.","A scanner's nominal accuracy holds at every range and angle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"10 個檢核點的殘差（mm）為 2.1、−1.5、3.0、−2.4、1.2、0.8、−2.9、1.9、−0.6、2.6，平方和 = 42.64，RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm，2σ 約 4.1 mm，落在 1 至 5 mm 的等級範圍內但接近上限。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Ten check-point residuals (mm) of 2.1, −1.5, 3.0, −2.4, 1.2, 0.8, −2.9, 1.9, −0.6 and 2.6 give a sum of squares of 42.64 and RMSE = √(42.64/10) = √4.264 ≈ 2.06 mm, a 2σ of about 4.1 mm, inside a 1 to 5 mm class but near its upper bound. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b098-v13-31","title":"掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「獨立檢核點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Independent check points” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"檢核點應分布在掃描範圍四周與中央、不同高度與距離，數量依面積訂定；每台掃描儀在專案開始前依 ISO 17123-9 做現場檢定並保存紀錄，檢核點結果與 LOA 規格一起列入交付報告，未達規格者重掃或補控制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Distribute check points around the edges and centre of the scanned area at different heights and ranges, with numbers set by area; test each scanner in the field to ISO 17123-9 before the project and keep the records, include check-point results with the LOA specification in the delivery report, and re-scan or add control where the specification is not met. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交付規格要求每個掃描區附獨立檢核點報告與儀器檢定紀錄，檢核點不得用於配準；監造驗收以檢核點結果為準，不接受只有軟體統計的成果。","observationEn":"Site practice: Delivery specifications require an independent check-point report and instrument test record for every scan area, with check points excluded from registration; the supervising engineer accepts on check-point results and rejects deliveries supported only by software statistics.","failure":"注意干擾：只以配準軟體顯示的「平均誤差 1 mm」作為精度證明，沒有任何獨立檢核；後來以全測站抽驗發現點雲整體旋轉，遠端偏差達 15 mm，已據以下料的帷幕牆托架必須重做。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using the registration software's ‘mean error 1 mm’ as the only proof of accuracy, with no independent checks, a later total-station spot check finds the cloud rotated so that far points are 15 mm out, and façade brackets already cut from it must be remade. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"檢核點應分布在掃描範圍四周與中央、不同高度與距離，數量依面積訂定；每台掃描儀在專案開始前依 ISO 17123-9 做現場檢定並保存紀錄，檢核點結果與 LOA 規格一起列入交付報告，未達規格者重掃或補控制。","textEn":"Distribute check points around the edges and centre of the scanned area at different heights and ranges, with numbers set by area; test each scanner in the field to ISO 17123-9 before the project and keep the records, include check-point results with the LOA specification in the delivery report, and re-scan or add control where the specification is not met.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交付規格要求每個掃描區附獨立檢核點報告與儀器檢定紀錄，檢核點不得用於配準；監造驗收以檢核點結果為準，不接受只有軟體統計的成果。","textEn":"Delivery specifications require an independent check-point report and instrument test record for every scan area, with check points excluded from registration; the supervising engineer accepts on check-point results and rejects deliveries supported only by software statistics.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","檢核點應分布在掃描範圍四周與中央、不同高度與距離，數量依面積訂定。","竣工掃描可以等全部完工後一次做完就好。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Distribute check points around the edges and centre of the scanned area at different heights and ranges, with numbers set by area.","As-built scanning can wait until everything is finished and be done once."],"answer":1,"explanation":"檢核點應分布在掃描範圍四周與中央、不同高度與距離，數量依面積訂定；每台掃描儀在專案開始前依 ISO 17123-9 做現場檢定並保存紀錄，檢核點結果與 LOA 規格一起列入交付報告，未達規格者重掃或補控制。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Distribute check points around the edges and centre of the scanned area at different heights and ranges, with numbers set by area; test each scanner in the field to ISO 17123-9 before the project and keep the records, include check-point results with the LOA specification in the delivery report, and re-scan or add control where the specification is not met. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b098-v13-32","title":"掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「獨立檢核點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Independent check points” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以配準軟體顯示的「平均誤差 1 mm」作為精度證明，沒有任何獨立檢核；後來以全測站抽驗發現點雲整體旋轉，遠端偏差達 15 mm，已據以下料的帷幕牆托架必須重做。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using the registration software's ‘mean error 1 mm’ as the only proof of accuracy, with no independent checks, a later total-station spot check finds the cloud rotated so that far points are 15 mm out, and façade brackets already cut from it must be remade. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：ISO 17123-9 規定以現場程序檢查地面雷射掃描儀的重複精度，可在專案開始前與定期檢查時使用；檢核結果再與 LOA 規格比較，決定成果能否用於判定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: ISO 17123-9 gives field procedures for checking the repeatability of terrestrial laser scanners, usable before a project and at periodic checks, and the check-point result is compared with the LOA specification to decide whether the data can support conformance decisions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「配準軟體報告的誤差就是點雲的絕對精度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The error reported by registration software is the absolute accuracy of the cloud.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以配準軟體顯示的「平均誤差 1 mm」作為精度證明，沒有任何獨立檢核；後來以全測站抽驗發現點雲整體旋轉，遠端偏差達 15 mm，已據以下料的帷幕牆托架必須重做。","textEn":"Using the registration software's ‘mean error 1 mm’ as the only proof of accuracy, with no independent checks, a later total-station spot check finds the cloud rotated so that far points are 15 mm out, and façade brackets already cut from it must be remade.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掃描精度驗證與儀器檢定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Verifying scan accuracy and testing scanners\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩期點雲直接相減，就能偵測到小於單點雜訊的變形。","只以配準軟體顯示的「平均誤差 1 mm」作為精度證明，沒有任何獨立檢核。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Subtracting two point clouds directly detects deformation smaller than single-point noise.","Using the registration software's ‘mean error 1 mm’ as the only proof of accuracy, with no independent checks, a later total-station spot check finds the cloud rotated so that far points are 15 mm out, and façade brackets already cut from it must be remade."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只以配準軟體顯示的「平均誤差 1 mm」作為精度證明，沒有任何獨立檢核；後來以全測站抽驗發現點雲整體旋轉，遠端偏差達 15 mm，已據以下料的帷幕牆托架必須重做。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using the registration software's ‘mean error 1 mm’ as the only proof of accuracy, with no independent checks, a later total-station spot check finds the cloud rotated so that far points are 15 mm out, and façade brackets already cut from it must be remade. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b098-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證」與「點雲資料管理、格式與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks\" and \"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b098-v13-33","title":"基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「災前基準掃描」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pre-event baseline scan” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"掃描成果在完工後仍有價值：它是日後變形監測的基準，也是災後重建的依據。藝術史學者 Andrew Tallon 自 2010 年起以雷射掃描記錄巴黎聖母院，2019 年大火後這批資料成為修復的參考；烏干達卡蘇比王陵在 2009 年被掃描，2010 年主陵毀於火災，這批紀錄被規劃作為重建依據。兩期掃描比對時，可偵測的最小變化不只取決於點的雜訊，更取決於兩期配準是否一致。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「災前基準掃描」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Scan data keeps its value after completion: it is the baseline for later deformation monitoring and the reference for rebuilding after disaster. The art historian Andrew Tallon laser-scanned Notre-Dame de Paris from 2010, and after the 2019 fire his data became a reference for restoration; the Kasubi Tombs in Uganda were scanned in 2009, their main tomb was destroyed by fire in 2010, and those records were intended to support reconstruction. When two epochs are compared, the smallest detectable change depends less on point noise than on whether the two registrations are consistent. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Pre-event baseline scan” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：每點雜訊 σ = 2 mm，取 100 點平均的區塊 σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm，兩期差值 σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm，95% 偵測門檻約 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With point noise σ = 2 mm, a patch averaging 100 points has σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm, the difference of two epochs σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm, and a 95% detection threshold of about 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩期點雲直接相減，就能偵測到小於單點雜訊的變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Subtracting two point clouds directly detects deformation smaller than single-point noise.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「災前基準掃描」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Pre-event baseline scan”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-33-k1","title":"基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證","titleEn":"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks","text":"掃描成果在完工後仍有價值：它是日後變形監測的基準，也是災後重建的依據。藝術史學者 Andrew Tallon 自 2010 年起以雷射掃描記錄巴黎聖母院，2019 年大火後這批資料成為修復的參考；烏干達卡蘇比王陵在 2009 年被掃描，2010 年主陵毀於火災，這批紀錄被規劃作為重建依據。","textEn":"Scan data keeps its value after completion: it is the baseline for later deformation monitoring and the reference for rebuilding after disaster. The art historian Andrew Tallon laser-scanned Notre-Dame de Paris from 2010, and after the 2019 fire his data became a reference for restoration; the Kasubi Tombs in Uganda were scanned in 2009, their main tomb was destroyed by fire in 2010, and those records were intended to support reconstruction.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩期點雲直接相減，就能偵測到小於單點雜訊的變形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Subtracting two point clouds directly detects deformation smaller than single-point noise. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks\" is correct?","options":["掃描成果在完工後仍有價值：它是日後變形監測的基準，也是災後重建的依據。","兩期點雲直接相減，就能偵測到小於單點雜訊的變形。","點雲交出檔案就完成交接，不需要後設資料。"],"optionsEn":["Scan data keeps its value after completion: it is the baseline for later deformation monitoring and the reference for rebuilding after disaster.","Subtracting two point clouds directly detects deformation smaller than single-point noise.","Handing over the point-cloud files completes the handover; metadata is unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"掃描成果在完工後仍有價值：它是日後變形監測的基準，也是災後重建的依據。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Scan data keeps its value after completion: it is the baseline for later deformation monitoring and the reference for rebuilding after disaster. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b098-v13-34","title":"基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「災前基準掃描」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pre-event baseline scan” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：每點雜訊 σ = 2 mm，取 100 點平均的區塊 σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm，兩期差值 σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm，95% 偵測門檻約 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm。若每期配準另有 1.5 mm 系統誤差，差值 σ = √(2×(0.2² + 1.5²)) ≈ 2.14 mm，門檻升到約 4.2 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With point noise σ = 2 mm, a patch averaging 100 points has σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm, the difference of two epochs σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm, and a 95% detection threshold of about 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm. If each epoch's registration also carries a 1.5 mm systematic error, the difference σ = √(2×(0.2² + 1.5²)) ≈ 2.14 mm and the threshold rises to about 4.2 mm. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：基準掃描要使用長期保留的控制點，並把控制點坐標、儀器、日期與配準報告一起保存；後續各期以同一組控制點定位，先比較穩定區域（例如基礎或未受影響的牆面）確認兩期一致，再解讀變化區域。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Baseline scans must use long-term control points, archiving their coordinates, the instrument, date and registration report together; later epochs are positioned on the same control, stable areas such as foundations or unaffected walls are compared first to confirm consistency, and only then are changed areas interpreted.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"每點雜訊 σ = 2 mm，取 100 點平均的區塊 σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm，兩期差值 σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm，95% 偵測門檻約 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm。若每期配準另有 1.5 mm 系統誤差，差值 σ = √(2×(0.2² + 1.5²)) ≈ 2.14 mm，門檻升到約 4.2 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With point noise σ = 2 mm, a patch averaging 100 points has σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm, the difference of two epochs σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm, and a 95% detection threshold of about 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm. If each epoch's registration also carries a 1.5 mm systematic error, the difference σ = √(2×(0.2² + 1.5²)) ≈ 2.14 mm and the threshold rises to about 4.2 mm. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks\", which statement holds?","options":["點雲精度很高，由它建立的模型自然也同樣精確。","每點雜訊 σ = 2 mm，取 100 點平均的區塊 σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm，兩期差值 σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm，95% 偵測門檻約 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm。","自動配準軟體顯示誤差很小，點雲位置就一定正確。"],"optionsEn":["If the point cloud is accurate, the model built from it is automatically just as accurate.","With point noise σ = 2 mm, a patch averaging 100 points has σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm, the difference of two epochs σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm, and a 95% detection threshold of about 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm.","If automatic registration reports small errors, the cloud must be correctly positioned."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每點雜訊 σ = 2 mm，取 100 點平均的區塊 σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm，兩期差值 σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm，95% 偵測門檻約 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With point noise σ = 2 mm, a patch averaging 100 points has σ = 2/√100 = 0.2 mm, the difference of two epochs σ = √2×0.2 ≈ 0.28 mm, and a 95% detection threshold of about 1.96×0.28 ≈ 0.55 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b098-v13-35","title":"基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「災前基準掃描」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pre-event baseline scan” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"基準掃描要使用長期保留的控制點，並把控制點坐標、儀器、日期與配準報告一起保存；後續各期以同一組控制點定位，先比較穩定區域（例如基礎或未受影響的牆面）確認兩期一致，再解讀變化區域。重建時從基準掃描抽取關鍵尺寸，與新建構件的掃描比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Baseline scans must use long-term control points, archiving their coordinates, the instrument, date and registration report together; later epochs are positioned on the same control, stable areas such as foundations or unaffected walls are compared first to confirm consistency, and only then are changed areas interpreted. In reconstruction, key dimensions are extracted from the baseline and compared with scans of the new work. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重要建築與文化資產應在完工或重大修復後建立基準掃描並納入資產紀錄，長期控制點與基準資料一起保存；變形判定結果須經結構工程師確認後才可發布。","observationEn":"Site practice: Important buildings and heritage assets should receive a baseline scan after completion or major restoration, kept in the asset record with the long-term control points; any deformation finding must be confirmed by a structural engineer before release.","failure":"注意干擾：兩期掃描各自以點雲匹配配準、沒有共同控制，比對結果顯示整座結構「傾斜」數毫米，引發不必要的緊急評估，查證後才發現只是兩期坐標系統不一致。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two epochs each registered by cloud matching without common control show the whole structure ‘tilting’ by several millimetres, triggering an unnecessary emergency assessment, until checking reveals that the two coordinate systems simply did not agree. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"基準掃描要使用長期保留的控制點，並把控制點坐標、儀器、日期與配準報告一起保存；後續各期以同一組控制點定位，先比較穩定區域（例如基礎或未受影響的牆面）確認兩期一致，再解讀變化區域。重建時從基準掃描抽取關鍵尺寸，與新建構件的掃描比較。","textEn":"Baseline scans must use long-term control points, archiving their coordinates, the instrument, date and registration report together; later epochs are positioned on the same control, stable areas such as foundations or unaffected walls are compared first to confirm consistency, and only then are changed areas interpreted. In reconstruction, key dimensions are extracted from the baseline and compared with scans of the new work.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重要建築與文化資產應在完工或重大修復後建立基準掃描並納入資產紀錄，長期控制點與基準資料一起保存；變形判定結果須經結構工程師確認後才可發布。","textEn":"Important buildings and heritage assets should receive a baseline scan after completion or major restoration, kept in the asset record with the long-term control points; any deformation finding must be confirmed by a structural engineer before release.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","樓板澆置完成後形狀就固定不變，何時量測都一樣。","基準掃描要使用長期保留的控制點，並把控制點坐標、儀器、日期與配準報告一起保存。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once a slab is poured its shape is fixed, so it does not matter when it is measured.","Baseline scans must use long-term control points, archiving their coordinates, the instrument, date and registration report together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基準掃描要使用長期保留的控制點，並把控制點坐標、儀器、日期與配準報告一起保存；後續各期以同一組控制點定位，先比較穩定區域（例如基礎或未受影響的牆面）確認兩期一致，再解讀變化區域。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Baseline scans must use long-term control points, archiving their coordinates, the instrument, date and registration report together; later epochs are positioned on the same control, stable areas such as foundations or unaffected walls are compared first to confirm consistency, and only then are changed areas interpreted. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b098-v13-36","title":"基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「災前基準掃描」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pre-event baseline scan” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩期掃描各自以點雲匹配配準、沒有共同控制，比對結果顯示整座結構「傾斜」數毫米，引發不必要的緊急評估，查證後才發現只是兩期坐標系統不一致。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two epochs each registered by cloud matching without common control show the whole structure ‘tilting’ by several millimetres, triggering an unnecessary emergency assessment, until checking reveals that the two coordinate systems simply did not agree. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：兩期掃描比對時，可偵測的最小變化不只取決於點的雜訊，更取決於兩期配準是否一致。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: When two epochs are compared, the smallest detectable change depends less on point noise than on whether the two registrations are consistent.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩期點雲直接相減，就能偵測到小於單點雜訊的變形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Subtracting two point clouds directly detects deformation smaller than single-point noise.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩期掃描各自以點雲匹配配準、沒有共同控制，比對結果顯示整座結構「傾斜」數毫米，引發不必要的緊急評估，查證後才發現只是兩期坐標系統不一致。","textEn":"Two epochs each registered by cloud matching without common control show the whole structure ‘tilting’ by several millimetres, triggering an unnecessary emergency assessment, until checking reveals that the two coordinate systems simply did not agree.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基準掃描、變形比對與重建驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Baseline scans, change detection and reconstruction checks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["兩期掃描各自以點雲匹配配準、沒有共同控制，比對結果顯示整座結構「傾斜」數毫米，引發不必要的緊急評估，查證後才發現只是兩期坐標系統不一致。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","點雲交出檔案就完成交接，不需要後設資料。"],"optionsEn":["Two epochs each registered by cloud matching without common control show the whole structure ‘tilting’ by several millimetres, triggering an unnecessary emergency assessment, until checking reveals that the two coordinate systems simply did not agree.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Handing over the point-cloud files completes the handover; metadata is unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩期掃描各自以點雲匹配配準、沒有共同控制，比對結果顯示整座結構「傾斜」數毫米，引發不必要的緊急評估，查證後才發現只是兩期坐標系統不一致。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two epochs each registered by cloud matching without common control show the whole structure ‘tilting’ by several millimetres, triggering an unnecessary emergency assessment, until checking reveals that the two coordinate systems simply did not agree. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b098-v13-37","title":"點雲資料管理、格式與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「E57 點雲檔與後設資料」如何影響建築雷射掃描竣工比對的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “E57 files and metadata” governs force, deformation or durability in “Laser-scan verification of as-built construction”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"點雲檔案很大且格式多樣，若只以掃描軟體的專有格式交付，業主日後可能無法讀取。ASTM E57 格式可在一個檔案中保存三維點、強度或顏色與影像，是常用的中立交換格式。交接時除了點雲本身，還要附上後設資料：坐標系統、控制點、儀器與日期、配準與檢核報告、LOA 等級；同時要管理資料量、版本與存取權限，以及掃描到的人員與敏感區域。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「E57 點雲檔與後設資料」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Point clouds are large and come in many formats, and delivery only in a scanning package's proprietary format may leave the owner unable to read them later. The ASTM E57 format stores three-dimensional points, intensity or colour and images in one file and is a common neutral exchange format. Handover needs metadata as well as the cloud: coordinate system, control points, instrument and date, registration and check reports, and LOA level, while data volume, versions, access rights and any captured people or sensitive areas must also be managed. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “E57 files and metadata” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：10 億點、每點以 3 個 4 位元組坐標加 2 位元組強度與 3 位元組顏色計 17 位元組，約 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB；若坐標以 8 位元組儲存，每點 29 位元組約 29 GB。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: One billion points at 17 bytes each (three 4-byte coordinates plus 2 bytes of intensity and 3 of colour) is about 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB; with 8-byte coordinates, 29 bytes per point gives about 29 GB.","failure":"常見誤解：「點雲交出檔案就完成交接，不需要後設資料。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Handing over the point-cloud files completes the handover; metadata is unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「E57 點雲檔與後設資料」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “E57 files and metadata”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-37-k1","title":"點雲資料管理、格式與交接","titleEn":"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover","text":"點雲檔案很大且格式多樣，若只以掃描軟體的專有格式交付，業主日後可能無法讀取。ASTM E57 格式可在一個檔案中保存三維點、強度或顏色與影像，是常用的中立交換格式。","textEn":"Point clouds are large and come in many formats, and delivery only in a scanning package's proprietary format may leave the owner unable to read them later. The ASTM E57 format stores three-dimensional points, intensity or colour and images in one file and is a common neutral exchange format.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：點雲交出檔案就完成交接，不需要後設資料。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Handing over the point-cloud files completes the handover; metadata is unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「點雲資料管理、格式與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover\" is correct?","options":["點雲交出檔案就完成交接，不需要後設資料。","點雲檔案很大且格式多樣，若只以掃描軟體的專有格式交付，業主日後可能無法讀取。","點雲有數百萬個點，所以每一點都比全測站量測更準確。"],"optionsEn":["Handing over the point-cloud files completes the handover; metadata is unnecessary.","Point clouds are large and come in many formats, and delivery only in a scanning package's proprietary format may leave the owner unable to read them later.","A point cloud has millions of points, so every point is more accurate than a total-station measurement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"點雲檔案很大且格式多樣，若只以掃描軟體的專有格式交付，業主日後可能無法讀取。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Point clouds are large and come in many formats, and delivery only in a scanning package's proprietary format may leave the owner unable to read them later. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b098-v13-38","title":"點雲資料管理、格式與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「E57 點雲檔與後設資料」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “E57 files and metadata” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：10 億點、每點以 3 個 4 位元組坐標加 2 位元組強度與 3 位元組顏色計 17 位元組，約 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB；若坐標以 8 位元組儲存，每點 29 位元組約 29 GB。三期掃描即 51 至 87 GB；抽稀保留 10% 作日常瀏覽約 1.7 至 2.9 GB。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: One billion points at 17 bytes each (three 4-byte coordinates plus 2 bytes of intensity and 3 of colour) is about 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB; with 8-byte coordinates, 29 bytes per point gives about 29 GB. Three epochs make 51 to 87 GB, and a 10% decimated copy for everyday viewing is about 1.7 to 2.9 GB. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交接前以第二套軟體開啟 E57 檔，確認坐標、強度與影像完整，並抽查控制點坐標與後設資料一致；檢查檔名與版本規則、備份與存取權限，並確認敏感區域已遮蔽或依規定處理。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before handover open the E57 files in a second software package to confirm coordinates, intensity and images are intact, and spot-check that control-point coordinates agree with the metadata; check naming and version rules, backups and access rights, and confirm that sensitive areas are masked or handled as required.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"10 億點、每點以 3 個 4 位元組坐標加 2 位元組強度與 3 位元組顏色計 17 位元組，約 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB；若坐標以 8 位元組儲存，每點 29 位元組約 29 GB。三期掃描即 51 至 87 GB；抽稀保留 10% 作日常瀏覽約 1.7 至 2.9 GB。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"One billion points at 17 bytes each (three 4-byte coordinates plus 2 bytes of intensity and 3 of colour) is about 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB; with 8-byte coordinates, 29 bytes per point gives about 29 GB. Three epochs make 51 to 87 GB, and a 10% decimated copy for everyday viewing is about 1.7 to 2.9 GB. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「點雲資料管理、格式與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["掃描儀的標稱精度在任何距離與角度都一樣。","竣工掃描可以等全部完工後一次做完就好。","10 億點、每點以 3 個 4 位元組坐標加 2 位元組強度與 3 位元組顏色計 17 位元組，約 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB。"],"optionsEn":["A scanner's nominal accuracy holds at every range and angle.","As-built scanning can wait until everything is finished and be done once.","One billion points at 17 bytes each (three 4-byte coordinates plus 2 bytes of intensity and 3 of colour) is about 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB."],"answer":2,"explanation":"10 億點、每點以 3 個 4 位元組坐標加 2 位元組強度與 3 位元組顏色計 17 位元組，約 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB；若坐標以 8 位元組儲存，每點 29 位元組約 29 GB。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"One billion points at 17 bytes each (three 4-byte coordinates plus 2 bytes of intensity and 3 of colour) is about 1×10⁹×17 = 17 GB; with 8-byte coordinates, 29 bytes per point gives about 29 GB. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b098-v13-39","title":"點雲資料管理、格式與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「E57 點雲檔與後設資料」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “E57 files and metadata” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交接前以第二套軟體開啟 E57 檔，確認坐標、強度與影像完整，並抽查控制點坐標與後設資料一致；檢查檔名與版本規則、備份與存取權限，並確認敏感區域已遮蔽或依規定處理。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before handover open the E57 files in a second software package to confirm coordinates, intensity and images are intact, and spot-check that control-point coordinates agree with the metadata; check naming and version rules, backups and access rights, and confirm that sensitive areas are masked or handled as required. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：合約要求以 E57 等中立格式加原生格式雙軌交付，附後設資料表與配準、檢核報告；業主資訊管理人員確認可讀後才簽收，並把點雲連結到資產資訊模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: The contract should require delivery in a neutral format such as E57 alongside the native format, with a metadata sheet and registration and check reports; the owner's information manager signs for it only after confirming readability, and links the cloud to the asset information model.","failure":"注意干擾：交付的點雲只有專有格式且沒有坐標系統說明，幾年後軟體授權失效、廠商不再支援，業主手上的資料等於無法使用，翻修時只能全部重新掃描。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Clouds delivered only in a proprietary format with no coordinate-system note become unusable years later when the licence lapses and the vendor no longer supports the format, so a renovation must scan everything again. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交接前以第二套軟體開啟 E57 檔，確認坐標、強度與影像完整，並抽查控制點坐標與後設資料一致；檢查檔名與版本規則、備份與存取權限，並確認敏感區域已遮蔽或依規定處理。","textEn":"Before handover open the E57 files in a second software package to confirm coordinates, intensity and images are intact, and spot-check that control-point coordinates agree with the metadata; check naming and version rules, backups and access rights, and confirm that sensitive areas are masked or handled as required.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"合約要求以 E57 等中立格式加原生格式雙軌交付，附後設資料表與配準、檢核報告；業主資訊管理人員確認可讀後才簽收，並把點雲連結到資產資訊模型。","textEn":"The contract should require delivery in a neutral format such as E57 alongside the native format, with a metadata sheet and registration and check reports; the owner's information manager signs for it only after confirming readability, and links the cloud to the asset information model.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「點雲資料管理、格式與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover\"?","options":["交接前以第二套軟體開啟 E57 檔，確認坐標、強度與影像完整，並抽查控制點坐標與後設資料一致。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","偏差圖大部分是綠色，就代表竣工品質合格。"],"optionsEn":["Before handover open the E57 files in a second software package to confirm coordinates, intensity and images are intact, and spot-check that control-point coordinates agree with the metadata.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If the deviation map is mostly green, the as-built quality is acceptable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交接前以第二套軟體開啟 E57 檔，確認坐標、強度與影像完整，並抽查控制點坐標與後設資料一致；檢查檔名與版本規則、備份與存取權限，並確認敏感區域已遮蔽或依規定處理。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before handover open the E57 files in a second software package to confirm coordinates, intensity and images are intact, and spot-check that control-point coordinates agree with the metadata; check naming and version rules, backups and access rights, and confirm that sensitive areas are masked or handled as required. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b098-v13-40","title":"點雲資料管理、格式與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"prerequisiteIds":["b098-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「E57 點雲檔與後設資料」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “E57 files and metadata” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"交付的點雲只有專有格式且沒有坐標系統說明，幾年後軟體授權失效、廠商不再支援，業主手上的資料等於無法使用，翻修時只能全部重新掃描。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Clouds delivered only in a proprietary format with no coordinate-system note become unusable years later when the licence lapses and the vendor no longer supports the format, so a renovation must scan everything again. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：交接時除了點雲本身，還要附上後設資料：坐標系統、控制點、儀器與日期、配準與檢核報告、LOA 等級；同時要管理資料量、版本與存取權限，以及掃描到的人員與敏感區域。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Handover needs metadata as well as the cloud: coordinate system, control points, instrument and date, registration and check reports, and LOA level, while data volume, versions, access rights and any captured people or sensitive areas must also be managed.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「點雲交出檔案就完成交接，不需要後設資料。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Handing over the point-cloud files completes the handover; metadata is unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b098-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"交付的點雲只有專有格式且沒有坐標系統說明，幾年後軟體授權失效、廠商不再支援，業主手上的資料等於無法使用，翻修時只能全部重新掃描。","textEn":"Clouds delivered only in a proprietary format with no coordinate-system note become unusable years later when the licence lapses and the vendor no longer supports the format, so a renovation must scan everything again.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]},{"id":"b098-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「點雲資料管理、格式與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Point-cloud data management, formats and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","交付的點雲只有專有格式且沒有坐標系統說明，幾年後軟體授權失效、廠商不再支援，業主手上的資料等於無法使用，翻修時只能全部重新掃描。","點雲有數百萬個點，所以每一點都比全測站量測更準確。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Clouds delivered only in a proprietary format with no coordinate-system note become unusable years later when the licence lapses and the vendor no longer supports the format, so a renovation must scan everything again.","A point cloud has millions of points, so every point is more accurate than a total-station measurement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"交付的點雲只有專有格式且沒有坐標系統說明，幾年後軟體授權失效、廠商不再支援，業主手上的資料等於無法使用，翻修時只能全部重新掃描。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Clouds delivered only in a proprietary format with no coordinate-system note become unusable years later when the licence lapses and the vendor no longer supports the format, so a renovation must scan everything again. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-usibd-loa","v13s-astm-e2807","v13s-unesco-kasubi","v13s-notre-dame-restoration","v13s-wiki-andrew-tallon"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
